module

public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.ExteriorPower.Basic
public import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.PiTensorProduct.Generators
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Kaehler.TensorProduct
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.TensorProduct.IsBaseChangeSpan

/-!
# The de Rham complex

Let `A → B` be a ring map of commutative rings, let `Ω[B⁄A]` be the module of Kähler
differentials of `B` over `A` with its universal `A`-derivation `d = KaehlerDifferential.D A B`,
and write `Ω^p_{B/A} = ⋀[B]^p Ω[B⁄A]` for the terms of the de Rham complex of `B` over `A`, with
the usual conventions `Ω^0_{B/A} = B` and `Ω^1_{B/A} = Ω[B⁄A]` (in Mathlib `⋀[B]^0 M ≃ B` via
`exteriorPower.zeroEquiv` and `⋀[B]^1 M ≃ M` via `exteriorPower.oneEquiv`).

For each degree `p` there is one and only one `A`-linear map `d : Ω^p_{B/A} → Ω^{p+1}_{B/A}` with

`d (b₀ · d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p) = d b₀ ∧ d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p`,

and these are the differentials of the de Rham complex.  Uniqueness holds because `Ω[B⁄A]` is
generated as a `B`-module by the elements `d b`, so that `Ω^p_{B/A}` is generated as an
`A`-module — indeed additively — by the elements `b₀ · d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p`.  Note that `d` is
`A`-linear and not `B`-linear: already in degree `0` the Leibniz rule gives
`d (b b') = b · d b' + b' · d b`.

Beyond their existence and uniqueness, two properties of these differentials are proved here.
The first is base change: for a second ring map `A → A'` and the pushout `B' = B ⊗_A A'`, the
`p`-th exterior power of `KaehlerDifferential.map A A' B B'` exhibits `Ω^p_{B'/A'}` as
`Ω^p_{B/A} ⊗_A A'`, compatibly with the differentials, so that `Ω^•_{B/A} ⊗_A A' = Ω^•_{B'/A'}`
as complexes.  The base change is along `A → A'` and not along `B → B'`, because the
differentials are `A`-linear only: `Ω^•_{B/A} ⊗_B B'` is not a complex, while
`Ω^•_{B/A} ⊗_A A'` is.  The second is descent along a quotient of the differentials: if
`π : Ω[B⁄A] → Ω` is a surjection of `B`-modules whose kernel is generated by elements `ω` with
`π ω = 0` and `(⋀^2 π) (d ω) = 0`, then the de Rham differentials descend uniquely to the
family `Ω^p = ⋀[B]^p Ω`, and the result is again a complex.

## Main definitions

* `KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential`: the de Rham differential
  `Ω^p_{B/A} → Ω^{p+1}_{B/A}` in degree `p`.
* `Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.SourceDeRham`: the de Rham complex of `B` over `A` in the
  form the descent of [Stacks, Tag 07HY] consumes, namely the
  family of `A`-linear differentials on the exterior powers of `Ω[B⁄A]` together with the
  defining rule on generators.
* `Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.sourceDeRham`: that complex, constructed — the de Rham
  differentials of `B` over `A` and their defining rule, so the structure above is inhabited
  rather than assumed.
* `Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.SourceDeRham.GenerationHypothesis`: `ker π` is generated by
  elements `ω` with
  `π ω = 0` and `(⋀^2 π) (d ω) = 0`, the hypothesis under which the differentials descend.

## Main results

* `KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D`: the displayed formula, satisfied by
  `deRhamDifferential p`.
* `KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_unique`: `deRhamDifferential p` is the only `A`-linear
  map on `⋀[B]^p Ω[B⁄A]` satisfying that formula.
* `KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_comp_self` and
  `KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_comp_deRhamDifferential`: **`d ∘ d = 0`**, the complex
  property of [Stacks, Tag 0FKF].
* `Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.comp_eq_zero_of_gen`: `d ∘ d = 0` follows from the defining
  rule on generators, so the `complex` field of `SourceDeRham` asks for nothing — that derivation
  is its default value.
* `Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.SourceDeRham.d_eq_deRhamDifferential` and
  `Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.SourceDeRham.eq_sourceDeRham`: the differentials of *any*
  `SourceDeRham A B` are the de Rham differentials, so that structure is a singleton, inhabited
  by `sourceDeRham A B`.
* `KaehlerDifferential.isBaseChange_exteriorPower_and_deRhamDifferential_comm`: the map
  `⋀^p (KaehlerDifferential.map A A' B B')` makes `Ω^p_{B'/A'}` the base change of
  `Ω^p_{B/A}` along `A → A'` in every degree `p`, and it is a map of complexes.
* `Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.SourceDeRham.exists_unique_quotient_deRhamDifferential`:
  under the generation hypothesis the differentials descend to `⋀[B]^p Ω`, uniquely, and the
  descended maps again form a complex.

## Implementation notes

Mathlib has no de Rham complex of a ring map, so there is no object for the differentials to be
fields of.  They are instead the standalone family `deRhamDifferential p`, which base change
refers to directly.  Descent reads its differentials off a `SourceDeRham`, a family subject to the
defining rule on generators; that is not a weakening, because the rule pins them down by
`deRhamDifferential_unique` — `SourceDeRham.eq_sourceDeRham` turns that into the statement that
`sourceDeRham A B` is the only term of the structure.  The complex property `d ∘ d = 0` is
therefore not something the structure asks for: `comp_eq_zero_of_gen` derives it from the rule,
and that derivation is the default value of the field `complex`, so no construction of a
`SourceDeRham` has to supply it.  `KaehlerDifferential.deRhamComplex` packages the same
differentials and the same square-zero theorem as a `CochainComplex`.

The differentials are constructed for every `p : ℕ` at once, where the source treats `p = 0` by
declaring `d : Ω^0_{B/A} → Ω^1_{B/A}` to be the universal derivation, `p = 1` by the presentation
of `Ω[B⁄A]` by the Leibniz relations, and `p ≥ 2` by factoring an alternating map on a tensor
power.  All three cases are replaced by one twisted module structure: the square-zero extension
`E[ε]` of `E = ⋀_B Ω[B⁄A]`, with `B` acting through the ring map `b ↦ b + ε · d b`.  A
`B`-multilinear map into `E[ε]` is a pair of an ordinary `B`-multilinear map and a map obeying the
Leibniz rule of the de Rham differential, so the universal properties of `Ω[B⁄A]` and of the
exterior power produce the differentials in degree one and in degree `p` respectively.  In degree
`0` the formula reads `d (b₀ · 1) = d b₀`, so the source's separate degree-`0` clause is the
`p = 0` case of the same statement rather than an exception to it.

`Ω^p_{B/A} ⊗_A A' = Ω^p_{B'/A'}` is spelled `IsBaseChange A' (ψ p)`, Mathlib's form of that
equality and the form of the degree-one case `KaehlerDifferential.isBaseChange` already in
Mathlib; `B' = B ⊗_A A'` is taken in the abstract form `Algebra.IsPushout A A' B B'`, so that the
statement applies to any ring realising the pushout.  Being a chain map is stated pointwise
rather than as an equality of composites, to avoid restricting the `A'`-linear `d' p` to an
`A`-linear map.  The ingredient the proof needs and Mathlib lacks is that taking exterior powers
commutes with base change; it rests on base change for alternating maps, whose one step with
content is that a bilinear map vanishing on the diagonal of an additively closed spanning set is
alternating.

## References

* [Stacks 0FKF](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FKF), the de Rham complex
* [Stacks 0FKG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FKG), formula (26): the differentials
* [Stacks 07HY](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07HY), descent along a quotient
* [Stacks 0H8Y](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0H8Y), base change of the complex
* [Stacks 00RV](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00RV), the degree-one case of base change,
  in Mathlib as `KaehlerDifferential.isBaseChange`
-/

namespace KaehlerDifferential

section Span

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- The wedges `d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p` of differentials of elements of `B` span `Ω^p_{B/A}` over `B`:
they are the wedges of the `B`-spanning set `Set.range (D A B)` of `Ω[B⁄A]`. -/
private lemma span_range_ιMulti_D_eq_top (p : ℕ) :
    Submodule.span B (Set.range fun c : Fin p → B ↦
      exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (c i)) = ⊤ := by
  have himg : exteriorPower.ιMulti B p ''
        {a : Fin p → Ω[B⁄A] | Set.range a ⊆ Set.range (D A B)} =
      Set.range fun c : Fin p → B ↦ exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (c i) := by
    refine Set.Subset.antisymm ?_ ?_
    · rintro _ ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
      choose c hc using fun i ↦ ha (Set.mem_range_self i)
      exact ⟨c, congrArg _ (funext hc)⟩
    · rintro _ ⟨c, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨_, Set.range_subset_iff.2 fun i ↦ ⟨c i, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
  rw [← himg, exteriorPower.ιMulti_span_of_span B p (Ω[B⁄A])
    (KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation A B)]

open Pointwise in
/-- The elements `b₀ · d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p` span `Ω^p_{B/A}` already as an `A`-module, not merely as
a `B`-module: they are `B • {d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p}`, and multiplying a `B`-spanning set by all of `B`
produces an `A`-spanning set. -/
private lemma span_range_smul_ιMulti_D_eq_top (p : ℕ) :
    Submodule.span A (Set.range fun b : Fin (p + 1) → B ↦
      b 0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (b i.succ)) = ⊤ := by
  have hset : (Set.univ : Set B) • (Set.range fun c : Fin p → B ↦
        exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (c i)) =
      Set.range fun b : Fin (p + 1) → B ↦
        b 0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (b i.succ) := by
    refine Set.Subset.antisymm ?_ ?_
    · rintro _ ⟨x, -, _, ⟨c, rfl⟩, rfl⟩
      exact ⟨Fin.cons x c, by simp⟩
    · rintro _ ⟨b, rfl⟩
      exact Set.smul_mem_smul (Set.mem_univ _) ⟨fun i ↦ b i.succ, rfl⟩
  rw [← hset, Submodule.span_smul_of_span_eq_top Submodule.span_univ,
    span_range_ιMulti_D_eq_top, Submodule.restrictScalars_top]


end Span

end KaehlerDifferential

open ExteriorAlgebra KaehlerDifferential

/-! ### Wedges in the exterior algebra -/

section ExteriorAlgebraAux

variable {R M : Type*} [CommRing R] [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M]

private lemma ι_mul_ι_swap (x y : M) : ι R x * ι R y = -(ι R y * ι R x) :=
  eq_neg_of_add_eq_zero_left (ExteriorAlgebra.ι_add_mul_swap x y)

/-- A vector, viewed in the exterior algebra, lies in the exterior power of degree one. -/
private lemma ι_mem_exteriorPower_one (x : M) : ι R x ∈ ⋀[R]^1 M := by
  simpa only [pow_one] using LinearMap.mem_range_self (ι R) x

/-- An element of degree two commutes with every vector: `⋀[R]^2 M` is spanned by the products
`ι u * ι v`, and moving `ι x` across such a product changes its sign twice. -/
private lemma mul_ι_comm_of_mem_exteriorPower_two {z : ExteriorAlgebra R M} (hz : z ∈ ⋀[R]^2 M)
    (x : M) : z * ι R x = ι R x * z := by
  have hz : z ∈ LinearMap.range (ι R) * LinearMap.range (ι R) := by rw [← pow_two]; exact hz
  refine Submodule.mul_induction_on hz ?_ ?_
  · rintro _ ⟨u, rfl⟩ _ ⟨v, rfl⟩
    rw [mul_assoc, ι_mul_ι_swap v x, mul_neg, ← mul_assoc, ι_mul_ι_swap u x, neg_mul, neg_neg,
      mul_assoc]
  · intro y w hy hw
    rw [add_mul, mul_add, hy, hw]

/-- A wedge of length one is the vector itself, read in the exterior algebra. -/
private lemma coe_ιMulti_one (x : M) :
    (exteriorPower.ιMulti R 1 (fun _ ↦ x) : ExteriorAlgebra R M) = ι R x := by
  rw [exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe, ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti_apply]
  simp

/-- A wedge of length one is additive in its entry, read in the exterior algebra. -/
private lemma coe_ιMulti_one_add (x y : M) :
    (exteriorPower.ιMulti R 1 (fun _ ↦ x + y) : ExteriorAlgebra R M)
      = (exteriorPower.ιMulti R 1 (fun _ ↦ x) : ExteriorAlgebra R M)
        + (exteriorPower.ιMulti R 1 (fun _ ↦ y) : ExteriorAlgebra R M) := by
  rw [coe_ιMulti_one, coe_ιMulti_one, coe_ιMulti_one, map_add]

/-- A wedge of length one is homogeneous in its entry, read in the exterior algebra. -/
private lemma coe_ιMulti_one_smul (c : R) (x : M) :
    (exteriorPower.ιMulti R 1 (fun _ ↦ c • x) : ExteriorAlgebra R M)
      = c • (exteriorPower.ιMulti R 1 (fun _ ↦ x) : ExteriorAlgebra R M) := by
  rw [coe_ιMulti_one, coe_ιMulti_one, map_smul]

/-- Prefixing a vector to a wedge multiplies by it, read in the exterior algebra. -/
private lemma coe_ιMulti_cons (n : ℕ) (x : M) (v : Fin n → M) :
    (exteriorPower.ιMulti R (n + 1) (Fin.cons x v) : ExteriorAlgebra R M)
      = ι R x * (exteriorPower.ιMulti R n v : ExteriorAlgebra R M) := by
  rw [exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe, exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe,
    ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti_succ_apply, Fin.cons_zero]
  rfl

/-- Prefixing a vector, as the `R`-bilinear map sending `(x, y) : M × ⋀[R]^q M` to the wedge
`x ∧ y : ⋀[R]^(q + 1) M`. -/
private noncomputable def wedgeι (q : ℕ) : M →ₗ[R] ⋀[R]^q M →ₗ[R] ⋀[R]^(q + 1) M :=
  LinearMap.mk₂ R (fun x y ↦ ⟨ι R x * (y : ExteriorAlgebra R M), by
      rw [add_comm]
      exact SetLike.mul_mem_graded (ι_mem_exteriorPower_one x) y.2⟩)
    (fun x₁ x₂ y ↦ Subtype.ext (by push_cast; rw [map_add, add_mul]))
    (fun c x y ↦ Subtype.ext (by push_cast; rw [map_smul, smul_mul_assoc]))
    (fun x y₁ y₂ ↦ Subtype.ext (by push_cast; rw [mul_add]))
    (fun c x y ↦ Subtype.ext (by push_cast; rw [mul_smul_comm]))

/-- `wedgeι` is multiplication by `ι R x`, read in the exterior algebra. -/
private lemma coe_wedgeι (q : ℕ) (x : M) (y : ⋀[R]^q M) :
    (wedgeι q x y : ExteriorAlgebra R M) = ι R x * (y : ExteriorAlgebra R M) := rfl

end ExteriorAlgebraAux

/-! ### The differentials of the de Rham complex -/

namespace DeRhamDifferential

section

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- The exterior algebra of `Ω[B⁄A]` over `B`: the de Rham complex of `B` over `A` lives in it. -/
private abbrev Ext (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] : Type _ :=
  ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])

private lemma ι_mul_ιMulti_eq_zero (n : ℕ) (v : Fin n → Ω[B⁄A]) (i : Fin n) :
    ι B (v i) * ιMulti B n v = 0 := by
  rw [ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti_apply]
  exact ExteriorAlgebra.ι_mul_prod_list v i

/-- The de Rham differential of a wedge of `n` differentials, as an `A`-multilinear map: the
antisymmetrisation of `d₁` over the `n` slots, written without signs. -/
private noncomputable def G (d1 : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[A] Ext A B) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, MultilinearMap A (fun _ : Fin n => Ω[B⁄A]) (Ext A B)
  | 0 => 0
  | (n + 1) =>
    LinearMap.uncurryLeft
      { toFun := fun ω => (LinearMap.mulLeft A (d1 ω)).compMultilinearMap
            (MultilinearMap.restrictScalars A (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti B n).toMultilinearMap) -
          (LinearMap.mulLeft A (ι B ω)).compMultilinearMap (G d1 n)
        map_add' := by
          intro ω ω'
          ext v
          simp only [map_add, sub_apply, LinearMap.compMultilinearMap_apply,
            LinearMap.mulLeft_apply, add_apply, add_mul]
          abel
        map_smul' := by
          intro a ω
          ext v
          simp only [map_smul, LinearMap.map_smul_of_tower, sub_apply,
            LinearMap.compMultilinearMap_apply, LinearMap.mulLeft_apply,
            smul_apply, RingHom.id_apply, smul_mul_assoc, smul_sub] }

private lemma G_zero (d1 : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[A] Ext A B) (v : Fin 0 → Ω[B⁄A]) : G d1 0 v = 0 := rfl

private lemma G_succ (d1 : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[A] Ext A B) (n : ℕ) (v : Fin (n + 1) → Ω[B⁄A]) :
    G d1 (n + 1) v =
      d1 (v 0) * ιMulti B n (Fin.tail v) - ι B (v 0) * G d1 n (Fin.tail v) := rfl

section Fixed

variable (d1 : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[A] Ext A B)
  (hsmul : ∀ (c : B) (ω : Ω[B⁄A]), d1 (c • ω) = c • d1 ω + ι B (D A B c) * ι B ω)
  (hD : ∀ b : B, d1 (D A B b) = 0)

include hsmul hD

/-- The differential in degree one lands in degree two: this holds on the generators `d b`, where
the value is `0`, and the Leibniz rule adds the degree-two term `d c ∧ d b'`. -/
private lemma d1_mem (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) : d1 ω ∈ ⋀[B]^2 (Ω[B⁄A]) := by
  have hmem : ω ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range (D A B)) := by
    rw [KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation A B]; exact Submodule.mem_top
  induction hmem using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy => obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hy; rw [hD]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ hy hz
  | smul c y _ hy =>
      rw [hsmul]
      refine Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hy) ?_
      exact SetLike.mul_mem_graded (ι_mem_exteriorPower_one _) (ι_mem_exteriorPower_one _)

/-- The values of the degree-one differential are central against vectors, having even degree. -/
private lemma d1_mul_ι_comm (ω x : Ω[B⁄A]) : d1 ω * ι B x = ι B x * d1 ω :=
  mul_ι_comm_of_mem_exteriorPower_two (d1_mem d1 hsmul hD ω) x

omit hsmul in
private lemma G_exact (n : ℕ) (b : Fin n → B) : G d1 n (fun i => D A B (b i)) = 0 := by
  induction n with
  | zero => exact G_zero d1 _
  | succ n ih =>
      have ht : Fin.tail (fun i : Fin (n + 1) => D A B (b i)) = fun i => D A B (b i.succ) := rfl
      rw [G_succ, hD, ht, ih fun i => b i.succ, zero_mul, mul_zero, sub_zero]

private lemma d1_mul_ιMulti (n : ℕ) (v : Fin n → Ω[B⁄A]) (k : Fin n) :
    d1 (v k) * ιMulti B n v = ι B (v k) * G d1 n v := by
  induction n with
  | zero => exact k.elim0
  | succ n ih =>
      have hv : ιMulti B (n + 1) v = ι B (v 0) * ιMulti B n (Fin.tail v) := ιMulti_succ_apply v
      induction k using Fin.cases with
      | zero =>
          rw [hv, G_succ, mul_sub, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc,
            d1_mul_ι_comm d1 hsmul hD, ExteriorAlgebra.ι_sq_zero, zero_mul, sub_zero]
      | succ j =>
          have hIH := ih (Fin.tail v) j
          have hzero : ι B (Fin.tail v j) * ιMulti B n (Fin.tail v) = 0 :=
            ι_mul_ιMulti_eq_zero n (Fin.tail v) j
          have hvj : v j.succ = Fin.tail v j := rfl
          rw [hvj, hv, G_succ, mul_sub, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc,
            ← d1_mul_ι_comm d1 hsmul hD, mul_assoc (d1 (v 0)), hzero, mul_zero,
            ι_mul_ι_swap (Fin.tail v j) (v 0), neg_mul, sub_neg_eq_add, zero_add,
            d1_mul_ι_comm d1 hsmul hD, mul_assoc, mul_assoc, hIH]

private lemma G_eq_zero_of_eq (n : ℕ) (v : Fin n → Ω[B⁄A]) (i j : Fin n) (hij : i ≠ j)
    (hv : v i = v j) : G d1 n v = 0 := by
  induction n with
  | zero => exact i.elim0
  | succ n ih =>
      induction i using Fin.cases with
      | zero =>
          induction j using Fin.cases with
          | zero => exact absurd rfl hij
          | succ j =>
              have hvj : v 0 = Fin.tail v j := hv
              rw [G_succ, hvj, d1_mul_ιMulti d1 hsmul hD n (Fin.tail v) j, ← hvj, sub_self]
      | succ i =>
          induction j using Fin.cases with
          | zero =>
              have hvj : v 0 = Fin.tail v i := hv.symm
              rw [G_succ, hvj, d1_mul_ιMulti d1 hsmul hD n (Fin.tail v) i, ← hvj, sub_self]
          | succ j =>
              have hij' : i ≠ j := fun h => hij (by rw [h])
              have hv' : Fin.tail v i = Fin.tail v j := hv
              rw [G_succ, ih (Fin.tail v) i j hij' hv',
                (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti B n).map_eq_zero_of_eq _ hv' hij']
              simp

omit hD in
private lemma G_update_smul (n : ℕ) [inst : DecidableEq (Fin n)] (c : B) (v : Fin n → Ω[B⁄A])
    (k : Fin n) :
    G d1 n (Function.update v k (c • v k)) =
      c • G d1 n v + ι B (D A B c) * ιMulti B n v := by
  obtain rfl : inst = instDecidableEqFin n := Subsingleton.elim _ _
  induction n with
  | zero => exact k.elim0
  | succ n ih =>
      have hv : ιMulti B (n + 1) v = ι B (v 0) * ιMulti B n (Fin.tail v) := ιMulti_succ_apply v
      induction k using Fin.cases with
      | zero =>
          have h0 : Function.update v 0 (c • v 0) 0 = c • v 0 := Function.update_self ..
          have ht : Fin.tail (Function.update v 0 (c • v 0)) = Fin.tail v :=
            Fin.tail_update_zero v _
          rw [G_succ, h0, ht, G_succ, hsmul, hv, map_smul, add_mul, smul_mul_assoc,
            smul_mul_assoc, smul_sub, mul_assoc]
          abel
      | succ k =>
          have h0 : Function.update v k.succ (c • v k.succ) 0 = v 0 :=
            Function.update_of_ne (Fin.succ_ne_zero k).symm _ _
          have ht : Fin.tail (Function.update v k.succ (c • v k.succ)) =
              Function.update (Fin.tail v) k (c • Fin.tail v k) := Fin.tail_update_succ v k _
          rw [G_succ, h0, ht, ih (Fin.tail v) k, G_succ, hv,
            (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti B n).map_update_smul, Function.update_eq_self, mul_add,
            mul_smul_comm, mul_smul_comm, smul_sub, ← mul_assoc, ← mul_assoc,
            ι_mul_ι_swap (v 0) (D A B c), neg_mul]
          abel

private lemma G_mem (n : ℕ) (v : Fin n → Ω[B⁄A]) : G d1 n v ∈ ⋀[B]^(n + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]) := by
  induction n with
  | zero => rw [G_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | succ n ih =>
      rw [G_succ]
      refine Submodule.sub_mem _ ?_ ?_
      · have hd : (n + 1 + 1) = 2 + n := by omega
        rw [hd]
        exact SetLike.mul_mem_graded (d1_mem d1 hsmul hD _)
          (by simpa using (exteriorPower.ιMulti B n (Fin.tail v)).2)
      · have hd : (n + 1 + 1) = 1 + (n + 1) := by omega
        rw [hd]
        exact SetLike.mul_mem_graded (ι_mem_exteriorPower_one _)
          (ih (Fin.tail v))

end Fixed
/-- The ring map `b ↦ b + ε · d b` from `B` into the square-zero extension `E[ε] = E ⊕ E · ε` of
`E = ⋀_B Ω[B⁄A]`.  It is multiplicative precisely because `d` is a derivation: the coefficient of
`ε` in `jetHom b * jetHom c` is `b · d c + c · d b`, and that is the Leibniz rule. -/
private noncomputable def jetHom (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] :
    B →ₐ[A] TrivSqZeroExt (Ext A B) (Ext A B) where
  toFun b := TrivSqZeroExt.inl (algebraMap B (Ext A B) b) + TrivSqZeroExt.inr (ι B (D A B b))
  map_one' := by simp
  map_mul' b c := TrivSqZeroExt.ext (by simp) (by
    have h : ι B (D A B b) * algebraMap B (Ext A B) c =
        algebraMap B (Ext A B) c * ι B (D A B b) := (Algebra.commutes _ _).symm
    simp [TrivSqZeroExt.snd_mul, Derivation.leibniz, Algebra.smul_def, h])
  map_zero' := by simp
  map_add' b c := TrivSqZeroExt.ext (by simp) (by simp)
  commutes' a := by simp [Algebra.algebraMap_eq_smul_one]

/-- `Jet A B` is the module of first-order jets of the exterior algebra `E = ⋀_B Ω[B⁄A]`: the
square-zero extension `E[ε]` with `B` acting through `jetHom`, so that its underlying `A`-module
is `E × E` while `b • (x, y) = (b x, b y + d b ∧ x)`.  A `B`-multilinear map into `Jet A B` is
therefore the same thing as a pair consisting of an ordinary `B`-multilinear map and a map obeying
the Leibniz rule of the de Rham differential; this is how both differentials constructed below
descend from multilinear algebra over `B`.  It is a synonym for `TrivSqZeroExt` rather than that
type itself because the `B`-action wanted here is the twisted one, not the one coming from the
`B`-algebra structure of `E`. -/
private def Jet (A B : Type*) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] : Type _ :=
  TrivSqZeroExt (Ext A B) (Ext A B)

namespace Jet

/-- The jet with value `x` and derivative `y`. -/
private def mk (x y : Ext A B) : Jet A B := (x, y)

/-- The value of a jet. -/
private def val : Jet A B → Ext A B := TrivSqZeroExt.fst

/-- The derivative of a jet. -/
private def der : Jet A B → Ext A B := TrivSqZeroExt.snd

private lemma ext {z w : Jet A B} (hv : val z = val w) (hd : der z = der w) : z = w :=
  TrivSqZeroExt.ext hv hd

@[instance_reducible] private noncomputable def addCommGroup : AddCommGroup (Jet A B) :=
  inferInstanceAs (AddCommGroup (TrivSqZeroExt (Ext A B) (Ext A B)))

attribute [local instance] Jet.addCommGroup

@[instance_reducible] private noncomputable def moduleA : Module A (Jet A B) :=
  inferInstanceAs (Module A (TrivSqZeroExt (Ext A B) (Ext A B)))

attribute [local instance] Jet.moduleA

@[instance_reducible] private noncomputable def moduleB : Module B (Jet A B) :=
  Module.compHom (TrivSqZeroExt (Ext A B) (Ext A B)) (jetHom A B).toRingHom

attribute [local instance] Jet.moduleB

private lemma fst_jetHom_mul (b : B) (w : TrivSqZeroExt (Ext A B) (Ext A B)) :
    (jetHom A B b * w).fst = b • w.fst := by
  simp [jetHom, Algebra.smul_def]

private lemma snd_jetHom_mul (b : B) (w : TrivSqZeroExt (Ext A B) (Ext A B)) :
    (jetHom A B b * w).snd = b • w.snd + ι B (D A B b) * w.fst := by
  simp [jetHom, TrivSqZeroExt.snd_mul, Algebra.smul_def]

private lemma val_mk (x y : Ext A B) : val (mk x y) = x := rfl

private lemma der_mk (x y : Ext A B) : der (mk x y) = y := rfl

private lemma val_add (z w : Jet A B) : val (z + w) = val z + val w := rfl

private lemma der_add (z w : Jet A B) : der (z + w) = der z + der w := rfl

/-- The value of a jet is `B`-linear: the twisted action does not disturb the first component. -/
private lemma val_smul (b : B) (z : Jet A B) : val (b • z) = b • val z :=
  fst_jetHom_mul b z

/-- The Leibniz rule, which is what the twisted `B`-action on the jets says. -/
private lemma der_smul (b : B) (z : Jet A B) :
    der (b • z) = b • der z + ι B (D A B b) * val z :=
  snd_jetHom_mul b z

private theorem isScalarTower : IsScalarTower A B (Jet A B) :=
  ⟨fun a b z => by
    have h : ∀ w : TrivSqZeroExt (Ext A B) (Ext A B),
        jetHom A B (a • b) * w = a • (jetHom A B b * w) := fun w => by
      rw [map_smul, smul_mul_assoc]
    exact h z⟩

attribute [local instance] Jet.isScalarTower

/-- The value of a jet, as a `B`-linear map. -/
private noncomputable def valMap : Jet A B →ₗ[B] Ext A B where
  toFun := val
  map_add' := val_add
  map_smul' := val_smul

/-- The derivative of a jet, as an `A`-linear map. -/
private noncomputable def derMap : Jet A B →ₗ[A] Ext A B where
  toFun := der
  map_add' _ _ := rfl
  map_smul' _ _ := rfl

end Jet

attribute [local instance] Jet.addCommGroup Jet.moduleA Jet.moduleB Jet.isScalarTower

open Jet

/-- The `A`-derivation `b ↦ (d b, 0)` of `B` with values in the jets of `⋀_B Ω[B⁄A]`.  The
universal property of `Ω[B⁄A]` applied to it is what produces the differential in degree one. -/
private noncomputable def jetD : Derivation A B (Jet A B) where
  toFun b := mk (ι B (D A B b)) 0
  map_add' b c := ext (by
      change ι B (D A B (b + c)) = ι B (D A B b) + ι B (D A B c)
      rw [map_add, map_add]) (by
      change (0 : Ext A B) = 0 + 0
      rw [add_zero])
  map_smul' a b := ext (by
      change ι B (D A B (a • b)) = a • ι B (D A B b)
      rw [Derivation.map_smul, LinearMap.map_smul_of_tower]) (by
      change (0 : Ext A B) = a • (0 : Ext A B)
      rw [smul_zero])
  map_one_eq_zero' := ext (by
      change ι B (D A B (1 : B)) = (0 : Ext A B)
      rw [Derivation.map_one_eq_zero, map_zero]) rfl
  leibniz' b c := by
    change mk (ι B (D A B (b * c))) 0 =
      b • (mk (ι B (D A B c)) 0 : Jet A B) + c • (mk (ι B (D A B b)) 0 : Jet A B)
    refine ext ?_ ?_
    · simp only [val_add, val_smul, val_mk, Derivation.leibniz, map_add,
        LinearMap.map_smul_of_tower]
    · simp only [der_add, der_smul, der_mk, val_mk, smul_zero, zero_add]
      exact (ExteriorAlgebra.ι_add_mul_swap _ _).symm

/-- The universal property of `Ω[B⁄A]` applied to `jetD`. -/
private noncomputable def jetLift : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[B] Jet A B :=
  Derivation.liftKaehlerDifferential jetD

/-- The de Rham differential in degree one, valued in the exterior algebra:
`d1 (b · d b') = d b ∧ d b'`. -/
private noncomputable def d1 : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[A] Ext A B :=
  derMap ∘ₗ jetLift.restrictScalars A

private lemma jetLift_apply_D (b : B) : jetLift (D A B b) = (mk (ι B (D A B b)) 0 : Jet A B) :=
  Derivation.liftKaehlerDifferential_comp_D jetD b

private lemma d1_apply_D (b : B) : d1 (D A B b) = (0 : Ext A B) := by
  show der (jetLift (D A B b)) = 0
  rw [jetLift_apply_D]
  rfl

private lemma val_liftKaehlerDifferential (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) :
    val (jetLift ω) = ι B ω := by
  have h : valMap ∘ₗ jetLift =
      (ι B : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[B] Ext A B) := by
    refine LinearMap.ext_on (KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation A B) ?_
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hx
    show val (jetLift (D A B b)) = ι B (D A B b)
    rw [jetLift_apply_D]
    rfl
  exact LinearMap.congr_fun h ω

private lemma d1_apply_smul (c : B) (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) :
    d1 (c • ω) = c • d1 ω + ι B (D A B c) * ι B ω := by
  show der (jetLift (c • ω)) =
    c • der (jetLift ω) + ι B (D A B c) * ι B ω
  rw [map_smul, der_smul, val_liftKaehlerDifferential]

/-- The alternating map `v ↦ (v 0 ∧ ⋯ ∧ v_{p-1}, G v)` with values in the jets.  It is
`B`-multilinear for the twisted action of `B` precisely because `G` obeys `G_update_smul`. -/
private noncomputable def jetAlternating (p : ℕ) : Ω[B⁄A] [⋀^Fin p]→ₗ[B] Jet A B where
  toFun v := mk (ιMulti B p v) (G d1 p v)
  map_update_add' v i x y := ext (by
      change ιMulti B p (Function.update v i (x + y)) =
        ιMulti B p (Function.update v i x) + ιMulti B p (Function.update v i y)
      exact (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti B p).map_update_add v i x y) (by
      change G d1 p (Function.update v i (x + y)) =
        G d1 p (Function.update v i x) + G d1 p (Function.update v i y)
      exact (G d1 p).map_update_add v i x y)
  map_update_smul' v i c x := ext (by
      simp only [val_mk, val_smul]
      exact (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti B p).map_update_smul v i c x) (by
      have h : Function.update v i (c • x) =
          Function.update (Function.update v i x) i (c • Function.update v i x i) := by
        rw [Function.update_self, Function.update_idem]
      simp only [der_mk, der_smul, val_mk]
      rw [h]
      exact G_update_smul d1 d1_apply_smul p c (Function.update v i x) i)
  map_eq_zero_of_eq' v i j hv hij := ext (by
      change ιMulti B p v = (0 : Ext A B)
      exact (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti B p).map_eq_zero_of_eq v hv hij) (by
      change G d1 p v = (0 : Ext A B)
      exact G_eq_zero_of_eq d1 d1_apply_smul d1_apply_D p v i j hij hv)

/-- The de Rham differential in degree `p`, valued in the exterior algebra. -/
private noncomputable def dp (p : ℕ) : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A]) →ₗ[A] Ext A B :=
  derMap ∘ₗ (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv (jetAlternating p)).restrictScalars A

private lemma dp_apply_ιMulti (p : ℕ) (v : Fin p → Ω[B⁄A]) :
    dp p (exteriorPower.ιMulti B p v) = G d1 p v := by
  show der (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv (jetAlternating p)
    (exteriorPower.ιMulti B p v)) = G d1 p v
  rw [exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv_apply_ιMulti]
  rfl

private lemma val_alternatingMapLinearEquiv (p : ℕ) (ξ : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    val (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv (jetAlternating p) ξ) = (ξ : Ext A B) := by
  have h : valMap ∘ₗ (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv (jetAlternating p)) =
      (⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])).subtype := by
    refine LinearMap.ext_on (exteriorPower.ιMulti_span B p (Ω[B⁄A])) ?_
    intro x hx
    obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := hx
    show val (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv (jetAlternating p)
      (exteriorPower.ιMulti B p v)) = ((exteriorPower.ιMulti B p v : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) : Ext A B)
    rw [exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv_apply_ιMulti]
    rfl
  exact LinearMap.congr_fun h ξ

private lemma dp_apply_smul (p : ℕ) (c : B) (ξ : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    dp p (c • ξ) = c • dp p ξ + ι B (D A B c) * (ξ : Ext A B) := by
  show der (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv (jetAlternating p) (c • ξ)) =
    c • der (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv (jetAlternating p) ξ) +
      ι B (D A B c) * (ξ : Ext A B)
  rw [map_smul, der_smul, val_alternatingMapLinearEquiv]

private lemma dp_mem (p : ℕ) (ξ : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) : dp p ξ ∈ ⋀[B]^(p + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]) := by
  have hξ : ξ ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range (exteriorPower.ιMulti B p)) := by
    rw [exteriorPower.ιMulti_span]; exact Submodule.mem_top
  induction hξ using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem y hy =>
      obtain ⟨v, rfl⟩ := hy
      rw [dp_apply_ιMulti]
      exact G_mem d1 d1_apply_smul d1_apply_D p v
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add y z _ _ hy hz => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ hy hz
  | smul c y _ hy =>
      rw [dp_apply_smul]
      refine Submodule.add_mem _ (Submodule.smul_mem _ _ hy) ?_
      have hd : p + 1 = 1 + p := by omega
      rw [hd]
      exact SetLike.mul_mem_graded (ι_mem_exteriorPower_one _) y.2

end

end DeRhamDifferential

namespace KaehlerDifferential

section

open DeRhamDifferential

variable {A B : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

/-- The de Rham differential `d : Ω^p_{B/A} → Ω^{p+1}_{B/A}` in degree `p`: the `A`-linear map
with `d (b₀ · d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p) = d b₀ ∧ d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p` for all `b₀, …, b_p ∈ B`, where
`d : B → Ω[B⁄A]` is the universal `A`-derivation.  That rule is
`deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D` and `deRhamDifferential_unique` says it pins the map down. -/
@[stacks 0FKG "the differential itself"]
public noncomputable def deRhamDifferential (p : ℕ) :
    ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A]) →ₗ[A] ⋀[B]^(p + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]) :=
  LinearMap.codRestrict (Submodule.restrictScalars A (⋀[B]^(p + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]))) (dp p) (dp_mem p)

private lemma coe_deRhamDifferential (p : ℕ) (ξ : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    (deRhamDifferential p ξ : Ext A B) = dp p ξ := rfl

/-- The defining rule of the de Rham differential:
`d (b₀ · d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p) = d b₀ ∧ d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p`.  The leading scalar `b₀` contributes the
factor `d b₀` through `dp_apply_smul`, and `G_exact` kills the wedge of exact forms. -/
@[stacks 0FKG "the defining rule of `deRhamDifferential`"]
public lemma deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D (p : ℕ) (b : Fin (p + 1) → B) :
    deRhamDifferential p (b 0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (b i.succ)) =
      exteriorPower.ιMulti B (p + 1) fun i ↦ D A B (b i) := by
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  rw [coe_deRhamDifferential]
  show dp p (b 0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i => D A B (b i.succ)) =
    ιMulti B (p + 1) fun i => D A B (b i)
  rw [dp_apply_smul, dp_apply_ιMulti, G_exact d1 d1_apply_D p fun i => b i.succ,
    smul_zero, zero_add]
  show ι B (D A B (b 0)) * ιMulti B p (fun i => D A B (b i.succ)) =
    ιMulti B (p + 1) fun i => D A B (b i)
  rw [ιMulti_succ_apply]
  rfl

/-- `deRhamDifferential p` is the only `A`-linear map `Ω^p_{B/A} → Ω^{p+1}_{B/A}` with
`d (b₀ · d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p) = d b₀ ∧ d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p`, because those elements span
`Ω^p_{B/A}` over `A`. -/
@[stacks 0FKG "uniqueness of `deRhamDifferential`"]
public theorem deRhamDifferential_unique (p : ℕ)
    (d : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A]) →ₗ[A] ⋀[B]^(p + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]))
    (hd : ∀ b : Fin (p + 1) → B,
      d (b 0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (b i.succ)) =
        exteriorPower.ιMulti B (p + 1) fun i ↦ D A B (b i)) :
    d = deRhamDifferential p :=
  LinearMap.ext_on (span_range_smul_ιMulti_D_eq_top p) <| by
    rintro _ ⟨b, rfl⟩
    rw [hd b, deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D p b]

/-- The de Rham differential kills a wedge `d c₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d c_p` of exact forms: it is the value of
the defining rule at `1 · d c₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d c_p`, a wedge with first factor `d 1 = 0`. -/
private lemma deRhamDifferential_ιMulti_D (p : ℕ) (c : Fin p → B) :
    deRhamDifferential (A := A) p (exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (c i)) = 0 := by
  have hz := deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D (A := A) (B := B) p (Fin.cons 1 c)
  simp only [Fin.cons_zero, Fin.cons_succ, one_smul] at hz
  rw [hz]
  exact (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (p + 1)).map_coord_zero (i := 0) (by simp)

/-- **The de Rham differential of `B` over `A` squares to zero.**  The elements
`b₀ · (d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_p)` span `Ω^p_{B/A}` over `A`, and on such an element the defining rule
computes the composite as a wedge whose first factor is `d 1 = 0`. -/
@[stacks 0FKF "the complex property d ∘ d = 0 of the de Rham complex of a ring map, on the \
exterior powers of the Kaehler differentials"]
public theorem deRhamDifferential_comp_self (p : ℕ) (ξ : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    deRhamDifferential (A := A) (p + 1) (deRhamDifferential p ξ) = 0 := by
  have hmem : ξ ∈ Submodule.span A (Set.range fun b : Fin (p + 1) → B ↦
      b 0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i ↦ D A B (b i.succ)) := by
    rw [span_range_smul_ιMulti_D_eq_top (A := A) (B := B) p]
    exact Submodule.mem_top
  induction hmem using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem v hv =>
      obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hv
      rw [deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D, deRhamDifferential_ιMulti_D]
  | zero => simp
  | add v w hv hw ihv ihw => rw [map_add, map_add, ihv, ihw, add_zero]
  | smul a v hv ih => rw [map_smul, map_smul, ih, smul_zero]

/-- **Consecutive de Rham differentials compose to zero**, as an equality of `A`-linear maps.
This is the complex property of the de Rham complex of `B` over `A`. -/
@[stacks 0FKF "the complex property d ∘ d = 0 of the de Rham complex of a ring map, as an \
equality of A-linear maps"]
public theorem deRhamDifferential_comp_deRhamDifferential (p : ℕ) :
    (deRhamDifferential (A := A) (B := B) (p + 1)).comp (deRhamDifferential p) = 0 :=
  LinearMap.ext fun ξ ↦ deRhamDifferential_comp_self p ξ

end

end KaehlerDifferential

/-! ### Base change of the de Rham complex -/

namespace DeRhamBaseChange

section IsAlt

variable {S N P : Type*} [CommSemiring S] [AddCommMonoid N] [Module S N]
  [AddCommMonoid P] [Module S P]

/-- A bilinear map vanishing on the diagonal of an additively closed spanning set is
alternating.  Additive closure is all that is used of the set: polarisation applied to
`x + y` gives antisymmetry on it, antisymmetry is a linear condition and hence holds on all
of `N`, and with `b` antisymmetric the `y` with `b y y = 0` form a submodule. -/
public lemma isAlt_of_span_eq_top {b : N →ₗ[S] N →ₗ[S] P} {s : AddSubmonoid N}
    (hs : Submodule.span S (s : Set N) = ⊤) (h : ∀ x ∈ s, b x x = 0) : b.IsAlt := by
  have hanti : b + b.flip = 0 :=
    LinearMap.ext_on hs fun x hx ↦ LinearMap.ext_on hs fun y hy ↦ by
      have h0 := h (x + y) (add_mem hx hy)
      simp only [map_add, LinearMap.add_apply, h x hx, h y hy, zero_add, add_zero] at h0
      simpa [add_comm] using h0
  intro y
  have hy : y ∈ Submodule.span S (s : Set N) := hs ▸ Submodule.mem_top
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem x hx => exact h x hx
  | zero => simp
  | add y z _ _ hy hz =>
    have h0 := DFunLike.congr_fun (DFunLike.congr_fun hanti y) z
    simp only [map_add, LinearMap.add_apply, hy, hz, zero_add, add_zero]
    simpa [add_comm] using h0
  | smul a y _ hy => simp [hy]

end IsAlt

/-- Two distinct points can be carried to any two distinct points by a permutation. -/
public lemma exists_perm_apply_eq {α : Type*} {i j k l : α} (hij : i ≠ j) (hkl : k ≠ l) :
    ∃ σ : Equiv.Perm α, σ i = k ∧ σ j = l := by
  classical
  have hτi : Equiv.swap i k i = k := Equiv.swap_apply_left i k
  have hτj : Equiv.swap i k j ≠ k := fun h ↦ hij ((Equiv.swap i k).injective (hτi.trans h.symm))
  refine ⟨(Equiv.swap i k).trans (Equiv.swap (Equiv.swap i k j) l), ?_, ?_⟩
  · rw [Equiv.trans_apply, hτi]
    exact Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne (Ne.symm hτj) hkl
  · rw [Equiv.trans_apply]
    exact Equiv.swap_apply_left _ _

section BaseChange

variable {R S M N : Type*} [CommRing R] [CommRing S] [Algebra R S]
  [AddCommGroup M] [Module R M] [AddCommGroup N] [Module R N] [Module S N]
  [IsScalarTower R S N]

variable {Q : Type*} [AddCommGroup Q] [Module R Q] [Module S Q] [IsScalarTower R S Q]

omit [Module R Q] [IsScalarTower R S Q] in
/-- Two `S`-multilinear maps on `N` agreeing on tuples from the image of `f` are equal. -/
public lemma multilinearMap_ext {n : ℕ} {f : M →ₗ[R] N} (hf : IsBaseChange S f)
    {β₁ β₂ : MultilinearMap S (fun _ : Fin n ↦ N) Q}
    (h : ∀ v : Fin n → M, (β₁ fun i ↦ f (v i)) = β₂ fun i ↦ f (v i)) : β₁ = β₂ :=
  MultilinearMap.ext_of_span_eq_top (γ := fun _ ↦ M) (g := fun _ m ↦ f m)
    (fun _ ↦ by simpa using IsBaseChange.span_range_eq_top hf) h

/-- An `R`-multilinear map on `M` extends to an `S`-multilinear map on the base change `N`,
one slot at a time: the extension in `n + 1` slots is the `S`-linear extension of the map
sending `x : M` to the extension of `α.curryLeft x`. -/
public lemma exists_multilinearMap {n : ℕ} {f : M →ₗ[R] N} (hf : IsBaseChange S f)
    (α : MultilinearMap R (fun _ : Fin n ↦ M) Q) :
    ∃ β : MultilinearMap S (fun _ : Fin n ↦ N) Q,
      ∀ v : Fin n → M, (β fun i ↦ f (v i)) = α v := by
  induction n with
  | zero =>
    refine ⟨MultilinearMap.constOfIsEmpty S _ (α 0), fun v ↦ ?_⟩
    rw [Subsingleton.elim (0 : Fin 0 → M) v]
    rfl
  | succ n ih =>
    have : IsScalarTower R S (MultilinearMap S (fun _ : Fin n ↦ N) Q) :=
      ⟨fun r s β ↦ by ext v; exact smul_assoc r s (β v)⟩
    choose F hF using fun x : M ↦ ih (α.curryLeft x)
    let F' : M →ₗ[R] MultilinearMap S (fun _ : Fin n ↦ N) Q :=
      { toFun := F
        map_add' := fun x y ↦ multilinearMap_ext hf fun v ↦ by
          simp only [hF, add_apply, MultilinearMap.curryLeft_apply]
          exact MultilinearMap.cons_add α v x y
        map_smul' := fun r x ↦ multilinearMap_ext hf fun v ↦ by
          simp only [hF, smul_apply, MultilinearMap.curryLeft_apply]
          exact MultilinearMap.cons_smul α v r x }
    refine ⟨LinearMap.uncurryLeft (M := fun _ : Fin (n + 1) ↦ N) (hf.lift F'), fun v ↦ ?_⟩
    have h1 : LinearMap.uncurryLeft (M := fun _ : Fin (n + 1) ↦ N) (hf.lift F')
        (fun i ↦ f (v i)) = F (v 0) (fun i ↦ f (v i.succ)) := by
      rw [LinearMap.uncurryLeft_apply, hf.lift_eq]
      rfl
    rw [h1, hF, MultilinearMap.curryLeft_apply]
    exact congrArg α (Fin.cons_self_tail v)

omit [IsScalarTower R S Q] in
/-- The multilinear extension of an alternating map vanishes on tuples whose first two
entries agree.  Read in its first two slots as a bilinear map with values in the multilinear
maps in the remaining slots, the extension vanishes on the diagonal of the image of `f`
because `α` is alternating, hence is alternating by `isAlt_of_span_eq_top`. -/
public lemma extension_eq_zero_of_zero_eq_one {m : ℕ} {f : M →ₗ[R] N}
    (hf : IsBaseChange S f) (α : M [⋀^Fin (m + 2)]→ₗ[R] Q)
    (β : MultilinearMap S (fun _ : Fin (m + 2) ↦ N) Q)
    (hβ : ∀ v : Fin (m + 2) → M, (β fun i ↦ f (v i)) = α v)
    (u : Fin (m + 2) → N) (hu : u 0 = u 1) : β u = 0 := by
  set b : N →ₗ[S] N →ₗ[S] MultilinearMap S (fun _ : Fin m ↦ N) Q :=
    (multilinearCurryLeftEquiv S (fun _ : Fin (m + 1) ↦ N) Q).toLinearMap ∘ₗ β.curryLeft
  have hb : ∀ (y z : N) (v : Fin m → N), b y z v = β (Fin.cons y (Fin.cons z v)) :=
    fun _ _ _ ↦ rfl
  have halt : b.IsAlt := by
    refine isAlt_of_span_eq_top (s := (LinearMap.range f).toAddSubmonoid)
      (by simpa [LinearMap.coe_range] using IsBaseChange.span_range_eq_top hf) ?_
    rintro _ ⟨x, rfl⟩
    refine multilinearMap_ext hf fun v ↦ ?_
    have hvec : (Fin.cons (f x) (Fin.cons (f x) fun i ↦ f (v i)) : Fin (m + 2) → N)
        = fun i ↦ f ((Fin.cons x (Fin.cons x v) : Fin (m + 2) → M) i) := by
      simp only [← Function.comp_def, Fin.comp_cons]
    rw [hb, hvec, hβ, zero_apply]
    exact α.map_eq_zero_of_eq _ (i := 0) (j := 1) (by simp) (by simp)
  have hvec : (Fin.cons (u 0) (Fin.cons (u 1) (Fin.tail (Fin.tail u))) : Fin (m + 2) → N) = u := by
    rw [show u 1 = Fin.tail u 0 by simp [Fin.tail], Fin.cons_self_tail, Fin.cons_self_tail]
  rw [← hvec, ← hu, ← hb, halt.self_eq_zero, zero_apply]

/-- Base change for alternating maps: an alternating `R`-multilinear map on `M` extends to an
alternating `S`-multilinear map on the base change `N`.  Any two slots of the extension can
be moved into the first two by a permutation, where `extension_eq_zero_of_zero_eq_one`
applies. -/
public lemma exists_alternatingMap {n : ℕ} {f : M →ₗ[R] N} (hf : IsBaseChange S f)
    (α : M [⋀^Fin n]→ₗ[R] Q) :
    ∃ β : N [⋀^Fin n]→ₗ[S] Q, ∀ v : Fin n → M, (β fun i ↦ f (v i)) = α v := by
  obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := exists_multilinearMap hf α.toMultilinearMap
  refine ⟨{ β with map_eq_zero_of_eq' := ?_ }, hβ⟩
  intro u i j hu hij
  obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ : ∃ m, n = m + 2 := by
    have hi := i.isLt
    have hj := j.isLt
    have : i.val ≠ j.val := fun h ↦ hij (Fin.ext h)
    exact ⟨n - 2, by omega⟩
  obtain ⟨σ, hσi, hσj⟩ := exists_perm_apply_eq hij (show (0 : Fin (m + 2)) ≠ 1 by simp)
  have hi' : σ.symm 0 = i := by rw [← hσi, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
  have hj' : σ.symm 1 = j := by rw [← hσj, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
  have key := extension_eq_zero_of_zero_eq_one hf (α.domDomCongr σ) (β.domDomCongr σ)
    (fun v ↦ hβ fun i ↦ v (σ i)) (u ∘ σ.symm) (by simp only [Function.comp_apply, hi', hj', hu])
  rw [MultilinearMap.domDomCongr_apply] at key
  simpa [Equiv.symm_apply_apply] using key

/-- Taking exterior powers commutes with base change: a map `Φ` in degree `n` compatible with
`ιMulti` and with a base change `f` in degree one is itself a base change. -/
public lemma isBaseChange_exteriorPower {n : ℕ} {f : M →ₗ[R] N} (hf : IsBaseChange S f)
    (Φ : ⋀[R]^n M →ₗ[R] ⋀[S]^n N)
    (hΦ : ∀ v : Fin n → M, Φ (exteriorPower.ιMulti R n v) =
      exteriorPower.ιMulti S n fun i ↦ f (v i)) :
    IsBaseChange S Φ := by
  refine IsBaseChange.of_lift_unique _ fun Q _ _ _ _ g ↦ ?_
  let _ := Module.addCommMonoidToAddCommGroup S (M := Q)
  obtain ⟨β, hβ⟩ := exists_alternatingMap hf (exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv.symm g)
  refine ⟨exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv β, ?_, fun g' hg' ↦ ?_⟩
  · refine exteriorPower.linearMap_ext ?_
    ext v
    simp only [LinearMap.compAlternatingMap_apply, LinearMap.coe_comp,
      LinearMap.coe_restrictScalars, Function.comp_apply, hΦ,
      exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv_apply_ιMulti, hβ,
      exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv_symm_apply]
  · refine LinearMap.ext_on
      (exteriorPower.ιMulti_span_of_span (R := S) (n := n) (M := N)
        (IsBaseChange.span_range_eq_top hf)) ?_
    rintro _ ⟨a, ha, rfl⟩
    choose v hv using fun i ↦ ha (Set.mem_range_self i)
    rw [show a = fun i ↦ f (v i) from funext fun i ↦ (hv i).symm,
      exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv_apply_ιMulti, hβ,
      exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv_symm_apply, ← hΦ]
    exact LinearMap.congr_fun hg' _

end BaseChange

/-- If `B' = B ⊗[A] A'` and `N` is the base change of the `B`-module `M` along `B → B'`,
then `N` is the base change of `M` along `A → A'`. -/
private lemma isBaseChange_restrictScalars_of_isPushout
    {A A' B B' : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing A'] [CommRing B] [CommRing B']
    [Algebra A A'] [Algebra A B] [Algebra A B'] [Algebra A' B'] [Algebra B B']
    [IsScalarTower A A' B'] [IsScalarTower A B B'] [Algebra.IsPushout A A' B B']
    {M N : Type*} [AddCommGroup M] [Module A M] [Module B M] [IsScalarTower A B M]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module A' N] [Module B N] [Module B' N]
    [IsScalarTower A A' N] [IsScalarTower A B N] [IsScalarTower B B' N] [IsScalarTower A' B' N]
    {f : M →ₗ[B] N} (hf : IsBaseChange B' f) :
    IsBaseChange A' (f.restrictScalars A) := by
  refine IsBaseChange.of_equiv
    ((Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange A A' B B' M).symm ≪≫ₗ hf.equiv.restrictScalars A') ?_
  intro x
  simp [hf.equiv_tmul]

/-- If `B' = B ⊗[A] A'`, then `Ω[B'⁄A']` is the base change of `Ω[B⁄A]` along `B → B'`.  This
is the companion of `KaehlerDifferential.isBaseChange`, which is the base change along
`A → A'`; both are Lemma 00RV. -/
private lemma isBaseChange_kaehlerDifferential_map
    {A A' B B' : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing A'] [CommRing B] [CommRing B']
    [Algebra A A'] [Algebra A B] [Algebra A B'] [Algebra A' B'] [Algebra B B']
    [IsScalarTower A A' B'] [IsScalarTower A B B'] [Algebra.IsPushout A A' B B'] :
    IsBaseChange B' (KaehlerDifferential.map A A' B B') := by
  refine IsBaseChange.of_equiv (KaehlerDifferential.tensorKaehlerEquiv A A' B B') ?_
  have key : (KaehlerDifferential.tensorKaehlerEquiv A A' B B').toLinearMap.restrictScalars B ∘ₗ
      TensorProduct.mk B B' (Ω[B⁄A]) 1 = KaehlerDifferential.map A A' B B' := by
    refine LinearMap.ext_on (KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation A B) ?_
    rintro _ ⟨b, rfl⟩
    simp
  exact fun x ↦ LinearMap.congr_fun key x

end DeRhamBaseChange

namespace KaehlerDifferential

open DeRhamBaseChange in
/-- **Stacks 0H8Y.** Let `A → A'` and `A → B` be ring maps, let `B' = B ⊗_A A'`, and let `ψ` be
the canonical map `⋀^p (KaehlerDifferential.map A A' B B')`.  Then `ψ` exhibits
`Ω^•_{B'/A'}` as the base change of `Ω^•_{B/A}` along `A → A'`, i.e.
`Ω^•_{B/A} ⊗_A A' = Ω^•_{B'/A'}`, and it is a map of complexes for the de Rham differentials
of `B` over `A` and of `B'` over `A'`. -/
@[stacks 0H8Y, ega "IV 16.6.4" "affine case"]
public theorem isBaseChange_exteriorPower_and_deRhamDifferential_comm
    {A A' B B' : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing A'] [CommRing B] [CommRing B']
    [Algebra A A'] [Algebra A B] [Algebra A B'] [Algebra A' B'] [Algebra B B']
    [IsScalarTower A A' B'] [IsScalarTower A B B'] [Algebra.IsPushout A A' B B']
    (ψ : ∀ p : ℕ, ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A]) →ₗ[B] ⋀[B']^p (Ω[B'⁄A']))
    (hψ : ∀ (p : ℕ) (ω : Fin p → Ω[B⁄A]),
      ψ p (exteriorPower.ιMulti B p ω) =
        exteriorPower.ιMulti B' p fun i ↦ map A A' B B' (ω i)) :
    (∀ p : ℕ, IsBaseChange A' ((ψ p).restrictScalars A)) ∧
      ∀ (p : ℕ) (ω : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])), ψ (p + 1) (deRhamDifferential p ω) =
        deRhamDifferential (A := A') (B := B') p (ψ p ω) := by
  refine ⟨fun p ↦ isBaseChange_restrictScalars_of_isPushout
    (isBaseChange_exteriorPower isBaseChange_kaehlerDifferential_map (ψ p) (hψ p)), fun p ↦ ?_⟩
  have key : ((ψ (p + 1)).restrictScalars A) ∘ₗ deRhamDifferential p =
      ((deRhamDifferential (A := A') (B := B') p).restrictScalars A) ∘ₗ
        ((ψ p).restrictScalars A) := by
    refine LinearMap.ext_on (span_range_smul_ιMulti_D_eq_top (A := A) (B := B) p) ?_
    rintro _ ⟨b, rfl⟩
    simp only [LinearMap.coe_comp, LinearMap.coe_restrictScalars, Function.comp_apply]
    rw [deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D p b, hψ (p + 1), map_smul, hψ p]
    simp only [KaehlerDifferential.map_D]
    have h := deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D (A := A') (B := B') p
      fun i ↦ algebraMap B B' (b i)
    simp only [algebraMap_smul] at h
    exact h.symm
  exact fun ω ↦ LinearMap.congr_fun key ω

end KaehlerDifferential

/-! ### Descending the de Rham complex along a quotient of the differentials -/

@[expose] public section

universe u

variable {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]

-- The `A`-module structures of this section live on the `RestrictScalars` synonyms `SrcA` and
-- `TgtA`; instance search and the rewrites below both have to unfold them, which they will not
-- do at reducible transparency.
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false

namespace Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent

/-- The `p`-th piece `Ω^p_{B/A} = ⋀^p_B Ω_{B/A}` of the source de Rham complex,
regarded as an `A`-module by restriction of scalars along `A → B` (the de Rham
differentials are `A`-linear but not `B`-linear). -/
abbrev SrcA (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] (p : ℕ) : Type u :=
  RestrictScalars A B (⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A]))

/-- The `p`-th piece `Ω^p = ⋀^p_B Ω` of the target graded family, as an
`A`-module by restriction of scalars. -/
abbrev TgtA (A B : Type u) [CommRing B] (Ω : Type u) [AddCommGroup Ω]
    [Module B Ω] (p : ℕ) : Type u :=
  RestrictScalars A B (⋀[B]^p Ω)

/-- The generator `b_0 · (d b_1 ∧ … ∧ d b_p) ∈ ⋀^p_B Ω_{B/A}`, where `d = D` is
the universal derivation; here `b : Fin (p+1) → B` lists `b_0, …, b_p`. -/
noncomputable def srcGen (p : ℕ) (b : Fin (p + 1) → B) : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A]) :=
  (b 0) • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p (fun i : Fin p => (KaehlerDifferential.D A B) (b i.succ))

/-- The value `d b_0 ∧ d b_1 ∧ … ∧ d b_p ∈ ⋀^{p+1}_B Ω_{B/A}`. -/
noncomputable def srcGenRes (p : ℕ) (b : Fin (p + 1) → B) : ⋀[B]^(p + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]) :=
  exteriorPower.ιMulti B (p + 1) (fun i : Fin (p + 1) => (KaehlerDifferential.D A B) (b i))

/-- A family of `A`-linear maps on the exterior powers of `Ω[B⁄A]`, read on the exterior powers
themselves rather than on their `RestrictScalars` synonyms `SrcA`. -/
private noncomputable def dPlain (d : ∀ p, SrcA A B p →ₗ[A] SrcA A B (p + 1)) (p : ℕ) :
    (⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) →ₗ[A] (⋀[B]^(p + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])) where
  toFun x := d p x
  map_add' x y := (d p).map_add x y
  map_smul' a x := (d p).map_smul a x

/-- **A family obeying the defining rule on generators is the family of de Rham differentials.**
`KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_unique` says the rule has exactly one solution, so the
rule leaves no choice. -/
theorem eq_deRhamDifferential_of_gen (d : ∀ p, SrcA A B p →ₗ[A] SrcA A B (p + 1))
    (hgen : ∀ p (b : Fin (p + 1) → B), d p (srcGen p b) = srcGenRes p b)
    (p : ℕ) (x : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    d p x = KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential (A := A) p x :=
  LinearMap.congr_fun
    (KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_unique p (dPlain d p) fun b => hgen p b) x

/-- **The complex property `d_{B/A} ∘ d_{B/A} = 0` is a consequence of the defining rule on
generators, not an independent demand.**  A family obeying the rule is the family of de Rham
differentials (`eq_deRhamDifferential_of_gen`), and those square to zero
(`KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_comp_self`, [Stacks, Tag 0FKF]). -/
theorem comp_eq_zero_of_gen (d : ∀ p, SrcA A B p →ₗ[A] SrcA A B (p + 1))
    (hgen : ∀ p (b : Fin (p + 1) → B), d p (srcGen p b) = srcGenRes p b) (p : ℕ) :
    (d (p + 1)).comp (d p) = 0 := by
  refine LinearMap.ext fun x => ?_
  rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearMap.zero_apply, eq_deRhamDifferential_of_gen d hgen p x,
    eq_deRhamDifferential_of_gen d hgen (p + 1) _]
  exact KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_comp_self p x

/-- The de Rham complex of `B` over `A` in the form the descent of Tag 07HY consumes: the family
of `A`-linear differentials `d_{B/A} : Ω^p_{B/A} → Ω^{p+1}_{B/A}` on the exterior powers of the
Kähler differentials, subject to the defining rule on generators.  That rule pins the family down
uniquely (`KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_unique`), so the structure is a singleton:
`Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.sourceDeRham` is a term of it and
`Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.SourceDeRham.eq_sourceDeRham` says it is the only one.  The
complex property `d_{B/A} ∘ d_{B/A} = 0` is therefore nothing the structure asks for: its field
`complex` is filled in by default from `comp_eq_zero_of_gen`, which derives it from `gen`. -/
structure SourceDeRham (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] where
  /-- The `A`-linear de Rham differentials `d_{B/A} : ⋀^p Ω_{B/A} → ⋀^{p+1} Ω_{B/A}`. -/
  d : ∀ p, SrcA A B p →ₗ[A] SrcA A B (p + 1)
  /-- The defining rule of Tag 0FKF on generators:
  `d_{B/A}(b_0 · d b_1 ∧ … ∧ d b_p) = d b_0 ∧ d b_1 ∧ … ∧ d b_p`. In particular,
  for `p = 0` this is the universal derivation `d_{B/A}(b_0) = D b_0`. -/
  gen : ∀ p (b : Fin (p + 1) → B), d p (srcGen p b) = srcGenRes p b
  /-- The complex property `d_{B/A} ∘ d_{B/A} = 0` of Tag 0FKF.  It never has to be supplied:
  `comp_eq_zero_of_gen` derives it from `gen`, and that derivation is this field's default
  value. -/
  complex : ∀ p, (d (p + 1)).comp (d p) = 0 := comp_eq_zero_of_gen d gen

/-- **The de Rham complex of `B` over `A`**, as a term of `SourceDeRham A B`: the de Rham
differentials `KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential` on the exterior powers of `Ω[B⁄A]`, which
obey the defining rule on generators by
`KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D`.  Nothing is supposed: the descent datum
of Tag 07HY is produced here, and its complex property is the theorem
`KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_comp_deRhamDifferential`, reached through the default
value of the field `complex`. -/
@[stacks 0FKF "the de Rham complex of a ring map A → B, as the family of A-linear differentials \
on the exterior powers of the Kaehler differentials together with the defining rule on \
generators and the complex property d ∘ d = 0; this construction has no hypothesis"]
noncomputable def sourceDeRham (A B : Type u) [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [Algebra A B] :
    SourceDeRham A B where
  d p := KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential (A := A) p
  gen p b := KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_smul_ιMulti_D (A := A) p b

namespace SourceDeRham

variable (S : SourceDeRham A B)

/-- **The differentials of a `SourceDeRham` are the de Rham differentials of `B` over `A`.**  The
field `gen` is the defining rule on generators and
`KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_unique` says that rule has exactly one solution, so the
structure carries no choice. -/
theorem d_eq_deRhamDifferential (p : ℕ) (x : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    S.d p x = KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential (A := A) p x :=
  eq_deRhamDifferential_of_gen S.d S.gen p x

/-- **A `SourceDeRham A B` is the de Rham complex of `B` over `A` and nothing else.**  Its
differentials are pinned down by the defining rule (`d_eq_deRhamDifferential`) and its other two
fields are propositions. -/
theorem eq_sourceDeRham : S = sourceDeRham A B := by
  obtain ⟨d, gen, cx⟩ := S
  have hd : d = (sourceDeRham A B).d :=
    funext fun p => LinearMap.ext fun x =>
      eq_deRhamDifferential_of_gen d gen p x
  subst hd
  rfl

variable {Ω : Type u} [AddCommGroup Ω] [Module B Ω] (π : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[B] Ω)

/-- A degree-`1` element `ω ∈ Ω_{B/A}` is a *good generator* of `ker π` when
`π ω = 0` and `(∧^2 π)(d_{B/A} ω) = 0`. Here `ω` is viewed in `⋀[B]^1 Ω_{B/A}`
via `oneEquiv.symm`, matching `Ω^1_{B/A} = Ω_{B/A}` and `∧^1 π = π`. -/
def GoodGenerator (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) : Prop :=
  π ω = 0 ∧
    exteriorPower.map 2 π (S.d 1 ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm ω)) = 0

/-- `ker π` is generated as a `B`-module by good generators. -/
def GenerationHypothesis : Prop :=
  LinearMap.ker π = Submodule.span B {ω : Ω[B⁄A] | S.GoodGenerator π ω}

/-- The target differential `d f := π (d_{B/A} f) ∈ Ω`. -/
noncomputable def targetD (f : B) : Ω := π ((KaehlerDifferential.D A B) f)

/-- The target generator `d f_0 ∧ d f_1 ∧ … ∧ d f_p ∈ ⋀^{p+1}_B Ω`, with
`d f = π (D f)` and `b : Fin (p+1) → B` listing `f_0, …, f_p`. -/
noncomputable def tgtGenRes (p : ℕ) (b : Fin (p + 1) → B) : ⋀[B]^(p + 1) Ω :=
  exteriorPower.ιMulti B (p + 1) (fun i : Fin (p + 1) => targetD π (b i))

/-- The target source-generator `f_0 · (d f_1 ∧ … ∧ d f_p) ∈ ⋀^p_B Ω`. -/
noncomputable def tgtGen (p : ℕ) (b : Fin (p + 1) → B) : ⋀[B]^p Ω :=
  (b 0) • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p (fun i : Fin p => targetD π (b i.succ))

/-- A candidate family of target differentials `dΩ : Ω^p → Ω^{p+1}` makes the
squares of Tag 07HY commute: `dΩ ∘ (∧^p π) = (∧^{p+1} π) ∘ d_{B/A}`. -/
def Commutes
    (dΩ : ∀ p, TgtA A B Ω p →ₗ[A] TgtA A B Ω (p + 1)) : Prop :=
  ∀ p (x : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])),
    dΩ p (exteriorPower.map p π x) = exteriorPower.map (p + 1) π (S.d p x)

/-- A candidate family satisfies the displayed rule on generators:
`dΩ(f_0 · d f_1 ∧ … ∧ d f_p) = d f_0 ∧ … ∧ d f_p`, `d f = π (D f)`. -/
def SatisfiesRule
    (dΩ : ∀ p, TgtA A B Ω p →ₗ[A] TgtA A B Ω (p + 1)) : Prop :=
  ∀ p (b : Fin (p + 1) → B), dΩ p (tgtGen π p b) = tgtGenRes π p b

end SourceDeRham

/-- A `B`-linear map read as an `A`-linear map between the `RestrictScalars` synonyms of its
source and target.  It is the identity on underlying elements. -/
private noncomputable def restrictScalarsMap {M N : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module B N] (g : M →ₗ[B] N) :
    RestrictScalars A B M →ₗ[A] RestrictScalars A B N where
  toFun := fun x =>
    (RestrictScalars.addEquiv A B N).symm (g (RestrictScalars.addEquiv A B M x))
  map_add' x y := by simp
  map_smul' a x := by
    simp only [RingHom.id_apply]
    rw [RestrictScalars.addEquiv_map_smul, map_smul]
    conv_rhs => rw [RestrictScalars.smul_def]
    simp

private theorem restrictScalarsMap_apply {M N : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M]
    [AddCommGroup N] [Module B N] (g : M →ₗ[B] N) (x : M) :
    restrictScalarsMap (A := A) g x = g x := rfl

/-- The factorisation of an `A`-linear map `f` through a surjective `A`-linear map `q` with
`ker q ≤ ker f`. -/
private noncomputable def liftOfSurjective {M N P : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [AddCommGroup N]
    [AddCommGroup P] [Module A M] [Module A N] [Module A P]
    (q : M →ₗ[A] N) (hq : Function.Surjective q) (f : M →ₗ[A] P)
    (h : LinearMap.ker q ≤ LinearMap.ker f) : N →ₗ[A] P :=
  (q.ker.liftQ f h).comp (LinearMap.quotKerEquivOfSurjective q hq).symm.toLinearMap

/-- Precomposing `liftOfSurjective q hq f h` with `q` recovers `f`. -/
private theorem liftOfSurjective_apply {M N P : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [AddCommGroup N]
    [AddCommGroup P] [Module A M] [Module A N] [Module A P]
    (q : M →ₗ[A] N) (hq : Function.Surjective q) (f : M →ₗ[A] P)
    (h : LinearMap.ker q ≤ LinearMap.ker f) (x : M) :
    liftOfSurjective q hq f h (q x) = f x := by
  unfold liftOfSurjective
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply]
  rw [show q x = LinearMap.quotKerEquivOfSurjective q hq (Submodule.Quotient.mk x) from rfl]
  rw [LinearEquiv.coe_coe, LinearEquiv.symm_apply_apply, Submodule.liftQ_apply]

namespace SourceDeRham

variable (S : SourceDeRham A B)
variable {Ω : Type u} [AddCommGroup Ω] [Module B Ω] (π : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[B] Ω)

/-- The `A`-linear projection `∧^p π : Ω^p_{B/A} → Ω^p`. -/
private noncomputable def mapA (p : ℕ) : SrcA A B p →ₗ[A] TgtA A B Ω p :=
  restrictScalarsMap (exteriorPower.map p π)

/-- On elements, the `A`-linear projection `∧^p π` is the `B`-linear `exteriorPower.map p π`. -/
private theorem mapA_apply (p : ℕ) (x : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    mapA π p x = exteriorPower.map p π x := rfl

/-- The `A`-linear projection `∧^p π : Ω^p_{B/A} → Ω^p` is surjective when `π` is. -/
private theorem mapA_surjective (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (p : ℕ) :
    Function.Surjective (mapA π p) :=
  exteriorPower.map_surjective hπ

/-- The composite `(∧^{p+1} π) ∘ d_{B/A} : Ω^p_{B/A} → Ω^{p+1}`. -/
private noncomputable def mapACompD (p : ℕ) : SrcA A B p →ₗ[A] TgtA A B Ω (p + 1) :=
  (mapA π (p + 1)).comp (S.d p)

/-- On elements, `mapACompD` is `(∧^{p+1} π) ∘ d_{B/A}`. -/
private theorem mapACompD_apply (p : ℕ) (x : SrcA A B p) :
    S.mapACompD π p x = exteriorPower.map (p + 1) π (S.d p x) := rfl

/-- The source de Rham differential annihilates a bare exact wedge
`D c_1 ∧ … ∧ D c_p ∈ ⋀^p`, the leading scalar being `1` and `D 1 = 0`. -/
private theorem d_ιMulti_D_eq_zero (p : ℕ) (c : Fin p → B) :
    S.d p (exteriorPower.ιMulti B p (fun i => (KaehlerDifferential.D A B) (c i))) = 0 := by
  rw [S.d_eq_deRhamDifferential]
  exact KaehlerDifferential.deRhamDifferential_ιMulti_D p c

/-- The defining rule of `S.d`, with the generators spelled out through `Fin.cons`. -/
private theorem d_smul_ιMulti_D (p : ℕ) (b₀ : B) (b : Fin p → B) :
    S.d p (b₀ • exteriorPower.ιMulti B p fun i => KaehlerDifferential.D A B (b i)) =
      exteriorPower.ιMulti B (p + 1)
        fun i => KaehlerDifferential.D A B ((Fin.cons b₀ b : Fin (p + 1) → B) i) :=
  S.gen p (Fin.cons b₀ b)

/-- The wedge `v ∧ w = ιMulti 2 ![v, w] ∈ ⋀^2 M` of two vectors, as a `B`-bilinear map. -/
private noncomputable def wedge2 {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M] :
    M →ₗ[B] M →ₗ[B] (⋀[B]^2 M) :=
  (wedgeι 1).compl₂ (exteriorPower.oneEquiv B M).symm.toLinearMap

/-- The bilinear wedge `wedge2 v w` is the degree-`2` generator `ιMulti 2 ![v, w]`. -/
private theorem wedge2_apply {M : Type u} [AddCommGroup M] [Module B M] (v w : M) :
    wedge2 v w = (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 2) ![v, w] := by
  refine Subtype.ext ?_
  show ι B v * ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B M).symm w : ExteriorAlgebra B M) = _
  rw [exteriorPower.oneEquiv_symm_apply, coe_ιMulti_one, exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe,
    ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti_apply]
  simp

/-- `oneEquiv` identifies `∧^1 π` with `π`. -/
private theorem oneEquiv_map (x : ⋀[B]^1 (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    exteriorPower.oneEquiv B Ω (exteriorPower.map 1 π x) = π (exteriorPower.oneEquiv B _ x) :=
  LinearMap.congr_fun (exteriorPower.oneEquiv_naturality π) x

/-- `d_{B/A}` carries `ker π` into `ker (∧²π)`: viewing `⋀^1 Ω_{B/A} = Ω_{B/A}` via `oneEquiv`,
for `x ∈ ⋀^1` with `(∧^1 π) x = 0` one has `(∧^2 π) (d_{B/A} x) = 0`. -/
private theorem map_d_eq_zero_of_one (hgen : S.GenerationHypothesis π)
    (x : ⋀[B]^1 (Ω[B⁄A])) (hx : exteriorPower.map 1 π x = 0) :
    exteriorPower.map 2 π (S.d 1 x) = 0 := by
  classical
  set D := KaehlerDifferential.D A B with hD
  set e := exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A]) with he
  have leib : ∀ ω : Ω[B⁄A], ∀ b : B,
      exteriorPower.map 2 π (S.d 1 (b • e.symm ω))
        = exteriorPower.map 2 π (wedge2 (D b) ω)
          + b • exteriorPower.map 2 π (S.d 1 (e.symm ω)) := by
    intro ω
    have hmem : ω ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range (KaehlerDifferential.D A B)) := by
      rw [KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation]; exact Submodule.mem_top
    induction hmem using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem v hv =>
        obtain ⟨c, rfl⟩ := hv
        intro b
        have hsymm : e.symm ((KaehlerDifferential.D A B) c)
            = exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => (KaehlerDifferential.D A B) c) := by
          rw [he]; exact exteriorPower.oneEquiv_symm_apply B (Ω[B⁄A]) _
        have hzero : S.d 1 (e.symm ((KaehlerDifferential.D A B) c)) = 0 := by
          rw [hsymm]
          exact S.d_ιMulti_D_eq_zero 1 (fun _ => c)
        have hsrc : b • e.symm ((KaehlerDifferential.D A B) c) = srcGen 1 ![b, c] := by
          rw [hsymm, srcGen]
          simp only [Matrix.cons_val_zero]
          congr 1
        have hwres : srcGenRes 1 ![b, c]
            = wedge2 ((KaehlerDifferential.D A B) b) ((KaehlerDifferential.D A B) c) := by
          rw [srcGenRes, wedge2_apply]
          congr 1
          funext i; fin_cases i <;> simp
        rw [hsrc, S.gen 1 ![b, c], hwres, hzero, map_zero, smul_zero, add_zero, hD]
    | zero =>
        intro b
        simp
    | add v w hv hw ihv ihw =>
        intro b
        rw [show e.symm (v + w) = e.symm v + e.symm w from map_add _ _ _,
          smul_add, map_add, map_add, ihv b, ihw b,
          show (wedge2 (D b)) (v + w) = wedge2 (D b) v + wedge2 (D b) w from map_add _ _ _]
        simp only [map_add, smul_add]
        abel
    | smul c v hv ih =>
        intro b
        have harg : b • e.symm (c • v) = (b * c) • e.symm v := by
          rw [map_smul, smul_smul]
        have harg2 : e.symm (c • v) = c • e.symm v := by rw [map_smul]
        rw [harg, harg2, ih (b * c), ih c]
        rw [map_smul, smul_add, smul_smul]
        rw [hD, Derivation.leibniz, map_add, map_smul, map_smul, map_smul]
        simp only [LinearMap.add_apply, LinearMap.smul_apply, map_add, map_smul]
        abel
  set ω₀ := e x with hω₀
  have hxsymm : x = e.symm ω₀ := by rw [hω₀, he]; simp
  have hπω₀ : π ω₀ = 0 := by rw [hω₀, he, ← oneEquiv_map, hx, map_zero]
  have hmem : ω₀ ∈ Submodule.span B {ω : Ω[B⁄A] | S.GoodGenerator π ω} := by
    rw [← hgen]; rw [LinearMap.mem_ker]; exact hπω₀
  rw [hxsymm]
  have key : ∀ ω : Ω[B⁄A], ω ∈ Submodule.span B {ω : Ω[B⁄A] | S.GoodGenerator π ω} →
      π ω = 0 ∧ exteriorPower.map 2 π (S.d 1 (e.symm ω)) = 0 := by
    intro ω hω
    induction hω using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem g hg =>
        refine ⟨hg.left, ?_⟩
        have := hg.right
        rw [he]; exact this
    | zero => simp
    | add v w hv hw ihv ihw =>
        refine ⟨by rw [map_add, ihv.left, ihw.left, add_zero], ?_⟩
        rw [map_add, map_add, map_add, ihv.right, ihw.right, add_zero]
    | smul c v hv ih =>
        refine ⟨by rw [map_smul, ih.left, smul_zero], ?_⟩
        rw [map_smul, leib v c, ih.right, smul_zero, add_zero]
        rw [hD, wedge2_apply, exteriorPower.map_apply_ιMulti]
        apply (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 2).map_coord_zero (i := 1)
        simp [ih.left]
  exact (key ω₀ hmem).right

/-- The coercion into the exterior algebra is additive on `SrcA A B n = ⋀^n_B Ω_{B/A}`:
restriction of scalars and `Submodule.subtype` are both the identity on elements. -/
private lemma coe_srcA_add (n : ℕ) (x y : SrcA A B n) :
    (((x + y : SrcA A B n) : ⋀[B]^n (Ω[B⁄A])).val : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      = ((x : ⋀[B]^n (Ω[B⁄A])).val : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
        + ((y : ⋀[B]^n (Ω[B⁄A])).val : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) := rfl

/-- The failure of the graded Leibniz rule in degrees `(1, q)` at the pair `(a, y)`, read inside
`ExteriorAlgebra B Ω_{B/A}` with `a` seen in degree `1` via `oneEquiv.symm`:
`d_{B/A}(a ∧ y) - ((d_{B/A} a) ∧ y - a ∧ (d_{B/A} y))`.  It is additive in each argument, so it
vanishes identically as soon as it vanishes on generators. -/
private noncomputable def leibnizDefect (q : ℕ) (a : Ω[B⁄A]) (y : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]) :=
  ((S.d (q + 1) (wedgeι q a y) : ⋀[B]^(q + 1 + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])).val : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
    - (((S.d 1 ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm a) : ⋀[B]^2 (Ω[B⁄A])).val
          : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) * (y : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      - (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => a) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
          * ((S.d q y : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])).val : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])))

private lemma leibnizDefect_zero_right (q : ℕ) (a : Ω[B⁄A]) : S.leibnizDefect q a 0 = 0 := by
  simp only [leibnizDefect, map_zero, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, mul_zero, sub_self]

private lemma leibnizDefect_zero_left (q : ℕ) (y : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    S.leibnizDefect q 0 y = 0 := by
  have h0 : (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => (0 : Ω[B⁄A])) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      = 0 := by rw [coe_ιMulti_one, map_zero]
  simp only [leibnizDefect, map_zero, LinearMap.zero_apply, ZeroMemClass.coe_zero, zero_mul]
  rw [h0, zero_mul, sub_self, sub_self]

private lemma leibnizDefect_add_left (q : ℕ) (a₁ a₂ : Ω[B⁄A]) (y : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    S.leibnizDefect q (a₁ + a₂) y = S.leibnizDefect q a₁ y + S.leibnizDefect q a₂ y := by
  simp only [leibnizDefect, map_add, LinearMap.add_apply, coe_srcA_add, coe_ιMulti_one_add,
    add_mul]
  abel

private lemma leibnizDefect_add_right (q : ℕ) (a : Ω[B⁄A]) (y₁ y₂ : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    S.leibnizDefect q a (y₁ + y₂) = S.leibnizDefect q a y₁ + S.leibnizDefect q a y₂ := by
  simp only [leibnizDefect, map_add, coe_srcA_add, Submodule.coe_add, mul_add]
  abel

/-- The graded Leibniz rule holds on generators: for `a = c · d e₀` and
`y = b₀ · (d b₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d b_q)` the defining rule of `S.d` computes all three differentials, the
Leibniz rule for `D (c · b₀)` matches the two leading scalars, and what is left of the identity is
the antisymmetry `d b₀ ∧ d e₀ ∧ ⋯ = - d e₀ ∧ d b₀ ∧ ⋯` of the exterior algebra. -/
private lemma leibnizDefect_smul_D_smul_ιMulti_D (q : ℕ) (c e0 b0 : B) (b : Fin q → B) :
    S.leibnizDefect q (c • KaehlerDifferential.D A B e0)
      (b0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti B q fun i => KaehlerDifferential.D A B (b i)) = 0 := by
  set D := KaehlerDifferential.D A B with hD
  set e := exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A]) with he
  have consD : ∀ (n : ℕ) (k : Ω[B⁄A]) (v : Fin n → Ω[B⁄A]),
      (ExteriorAlgebra.ι B k) * (exteriorPower.ιMulti B n v : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
        = (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (n+1) (Fin.cons k v) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) :=
    fun n k v => (coe_ιMulti_cons n k v).symm
  set W := exteriorPower.ιMulti B q (fun i => D (b i)) with hW
  have hT2 : S.d q (b0 • W)
      = exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (fun i => D ((Fin.cons b0 b : Fin (q+1) → B) i)) :=
    S.d_smul_ιMulti_D q b0 b
  have hT1 : S.d 1 (e.symm (c • D e0))
      = exteriorPower.ιMulti B 2 (fun i => D ((![c, e0] : Fin 2 → B) i)) := by
    have hsrc : e.symm (c • D e0) = srcGen 1 ![c, e0] := by
      rw [srcGen, he, map_smul, exteriorPower.oneEquiv_symm_apply]
      simp only [Matrix.cons_val_zero]; rfl
    rw [hsrc, S.gen 1 ![c, e0], srcGenRes]
  have hLHS : S.d (q+1)
      ((c * b0) • exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (fun i => D ((Fin.cons e0 b : Fin (q+1) → B) i)))
      = exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+2)
          (fun i => D ((Fin.cons (c*b0) (Fin.cons e0 b) : Fin (q+2) → B) i)) :=
    S.d_smul_ιMulti_D (q+1) (c*b0) (Fin.cons e0 b)
  have hDcons : ∀ (x : B) (n : ℕ) (v : Fin n → B),
      (fun i => D ((Fin.cons x v : Fin (n+1) → B) i)) = Fin.cons (D x) (fun i => D (v i)) := by
    intro x n v; funext i; refine Fin.cases ?_ ?_ i <;> simp
  have hwedeq : wedgeι q (c • D e0) (b0 • W)
      = (c * b0) • exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1)
          (fun i => D ((Fin.cons e0 b : Fin (q+1) → B) i)) := by
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    rw [coe_wedgeι, map_smul, hW]
    push_cast
    rw [smul_mul_assoc, mul_smul_comm, consD q (D e0) (fun i => D (b i)), hDcons e0 q b,
      smul_smul]
  set Ta := (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+2)
    (Fin.cons (D b0) (Fin.cons (D e0) (fun i => D (b i)))) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) with hTa
  set Tb := (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+2)
    (Fin.cons (D c) (Fin.cons (D e0) (fun i => D (b i)))) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) with hTb
  set Td := (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+2)
    (Fin.cons (D e0) (Fin.cons (D b0) (fun i => D (b i)))) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) with hTd
  have hLHSexp : (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+2)
      (fun i => D ((Fin.cons (c*b0) (Fin.cons e0 b) : Fin (q+2) → B) i))
        : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      = c • Ta + b0 • Tb := by
    rw [hDcons (c*b0) (q+1) (Fin.cons e0 b)]
    rw [← consD (q+1) (D (c*b0)) (fun i => D ((Fin.cons e0 b : Fin (q+1) → B) i))]
    rw [hD, Derivation.leibniz, map_add, map_smul, map_smul]
    rw [add_mul, smul_mul_assoc, smul_mul_assoc]
    rw [consD (q+1) (D b0) (fun i => D ((Fin.cons e0 b : Fin (q+1) → B) i)),
        consD (q+1) (D c) (fun i => D ((Fin.cons e0 b : Fin (q+1) → B) i))]
    rw [hTa, hTb, hDcons e0 q b]
  have hT1prod : (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 2 (fun i => D ((![c, e0] : Fin 2 → B) i))
      : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      * ((b0 • W : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) = b0 • Tb := by
    rw [hW]
    rw [show ((b0 • exteriorPower.ιMulti B q (fun i => D (b i)) : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A]))
          : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
        = b0 • (exteriorPower.ιMulti B q (fun i => D (b i)) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
            by push_cast; ring_nf]
    rw [show (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 2 (fun i => D ((![c, e0] : Fin 2 → B) i))
          : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
        = ExteriorAlgebra.ι B (D c) * ExteriorAlgebra.ι B (D e0) by
      rw [exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe, ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti_apply, List.ofFn_succ,
        List.ofFn_succ, List.ofFn_zero]; simp]
    rw [mul_smul_comm, mul_assoc, consD q (D e0) (fun i => D (b i)),
      consD (q+1) (D c) (Fin.cons (D e0) (fun i => D (b i)))]
  have hT2prod : (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => c • D e0) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      * (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (fun i => D ((Fin.cons b0 b : Fin (q+1) → B) i))
          : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) = c • Td := by
    rw [coe_ιMulti_one_smul, coe_ιMulti_one, smul_mul_assoc, hDcons b0 q b,
      consD (q+1) (D e0) (Fin.cons (D b0) (fun i => D (b i)))]
  have hTaTd : Ta = - Td := by
    rw [hTa, hTd]
    rw [exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe, exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe]
    have h01 : (0 : Fin (q+2)) ≠ 1 := by
      rw [Ne, Fin.ext_iff]; simp
    have hswap := (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti B (q+2)).map_swap
      (Fin.cons (D e0) (Fin.cons (D b0) (fun i => D (b i)))) (i := 0) (j := 1) h01
    rw [← hswap]
    congr 1
    funext i
    refine Fin.cases ?_ ?_ i
    · simp [Equiv.swap_apply_left]
    · intro j
      refine Fin.cases ?_ ?_ j
      · simp [Equiv.swap_apply_right]
      · intro k
        rw [Function.comp_apply]
        rw [show Equiv.swap (0 : Fin (q+2)) 1 k.succ.succ = k.succ.succ from
          Equiv.swap_apply_of_ne_of_ne (by simp [Fin.ext_iff]) (by simp [Fin.ext_iff])]
        simp
  show ((S.d (q + 1) (wedgeι q (c • D e0) (b0 • W)) : ⋀[B]^(q + 1 + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])).val
      : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      - (((S.d 1 (e.symm (c • D e0)) : ⋀[B]^2 (Ω[B⁄A])).val : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
          * ((b0 • W : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
        - (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => c • D e0) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
            * ((S.d q (b0 • W) : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])).val
                : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))) = 0
  rw [hwedeq, hLHS, hT1, hT2, hLHSexp, hT1prod, hT2prod, hTaTd]
  rw [smul_neg]; abel
/-- The graded Leibniz rule in degrees `(1, q)`, in the form that the defect vanishes: it is
additive in each argument, and the `B`-module generators of `Ω_{B/A}` and of `⋀^q_B Ω_{B/A}` are
the pairs settled by `leibnizDefect_smul_D_smul_ιMulti_D`.  A scalar is absorbed into a generator
rather than pulled out, since the defect is additive but not homogeneous. -/
private lemma leibnizDefect_eq_zero (q : ℕ) (a : Ω[B⁄A]) (y : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])) :
    S.leibnizDefect q a y = 0 := by
  set D := KaehlerDifferential.D A B with hD
  have Dwedge_span : Submodule.span B (Set.range (fun b : Fin q → B =>
      exteriorPower.ιMulti B q (fun i => D (b i)))) = (⊤ : Submodule B (⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A]))) := by
    rw [hD]; exact span_range_ιMulti_D_eq_top q
  have mainζ : ∀ (c : B) (e0 : B) (y : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])),
      S.leibnizDefect q (c • D e0) y = 0 := by
    intro c e0 y
    have hspan : y ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range (fun b : Fin q → B =>
        exteriorPower.ιMulti B q (fun i => D (b i)))) := by
      rw [Dwedge_span]; exact Submodule.mem_top
    suffices H : ∀ y' ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range (fun b : Fin q → B =>
        exteriorPower.ιMulti B q (fun i => D (b i)))),
        ∀ (b0 : B), S.leibnizDefect q (c • D e0) (b0 • y') = 0 by
      have := H y hspan 1; rwa [one_smul] at this
    intro y' hy'
    induction hy' using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem v hv =>
        obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := hv
        intro b0; exact S.leibnizDefect_smul_D_smul_ιMulti_D q c e0 b0 b
    | zero => intro b0; rw [smul_zero, S.leibnizDefect_zero_right]
    | add v w hv hw ihv ihw =>
        intro b0; rw [smul_add, S.leibnizDefect_add_right, ihv b0, ihw b0, add_zero]
    | smul d v hv ih =>
        intro b0; rw [smul_smul, ih (b0 * d)]
  have hspan : a ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range D) := by
    rw [KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation]; exact Submodule.mem_top
  suffices H : ∀ a' ∈ Submodule.span B (Set.range D),
      ∀ (c : B) (y : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])), S.leibnizDefect q (c • a') y = 0 by
    have := H a hspan 1 y; rwa [one_smul] at this
  intro a' ha'
  induction ha' using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem v hv =>
      obtain ⟨e0, rfl⟩ := hv
      intro c y; exact mainζ c e0 y
  | zero => intro c y; rw [smul_zero, S.leibnizDefect_zero_left]
  | add v w hv hw ihv ihw =>
      intro c y; rw [smul_add, S.leibnizDefect_add_left, ihv c y, ihw c y, add_zero]
  | smul d v hv ih =>
      intro c y; rw [smul_smul, ih (c * d) y]

/-- The graded Leibniz rule in degrees `(1, q)`: for `ω : Ω_{B/A}`, seen in degree `1` via
`oneEquiv.symm`, and `ζ : ⋀^q`, with `z : ⋀^{q+1}` the wedge `ω ∧ ζ`,
`d_{B/A}(ω ∧ ζ) = (d_{B/A} ω) ∧ ζ − ω ∧ (d_{B/A} ζ)`, the sign being `(-1)^{deg ω} = -1`.
Both the hypothesis on `z` and the conclusion are stated inside `ExteriorAlgebra B Ω_{B/A}`,
where no degree coercion intervenes; the coercion `↑ : ⋀^n → ExteriorAlgebra` is
`Submodule.subtype`, hence injective, so this is equivalent to the graded equation. -/
private theorem coe_d_wedge_one (q : ℕ) (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) (ζ : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A]))
    (z : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]))
    (hz : (z : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      = (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
          * (ζ : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))) :
    ((S.d (q + 1) z : ⋀[B]^(q + 1 + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])).1 : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      = ((S.d 1 ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm ω) : ⋀[B]^2 (Ω[B⁄A])).1
          : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) * (ζ : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
        - (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
            * ((S.d q ζ : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])).1 : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) := by
  have hzeq : z = wedgeι q ω ζ := by
    refine Subtype.ext ?_
    rw [hz, coe_wedgeι, coe_ιMulti_one]
  rw [hzeq]
  exact eq_of_sub_eq_zero (S.leibnizDefect_eq_zero q ω ζ)

/-- `ker (∧^{q+1} π)` is spanned over `B` by the wedges `ω ∧ ζ` whose first factor lies in
`ker π`; this is the right-exactness of the exterior power. -/
private theorem ker_exteriorPower_map_le_span (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (q : ℕ) :
    LinearMap.ker (exteriorPower.map (q + 1) π) ≤
      Submodule.span B
        {z : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]) |
          ∃ (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) (ζ : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])), π ω = 0 ∧
            (z : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
              = (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
                  * (ζ : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))} := by
  classical
  set Nsub := Submodule.span B {z : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]) |
      ∃ (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) (ζ : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])), π ω = 0 ∧
        (z : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
          = (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
              * (ζ : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))}
  set sec := Function.surjInv hπ
  have hs : ∀ w, π (sec w) = w := fun w => Function.surjInv_eq hπ w
  have memN_slot : ∀ (u : Fin (q+1) → Ω[B⁄A]) (i : Fin (q+1)), u i ∈ LinearMap.ker π →
      exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) u ∈ Nsub := by
    intro u i hi
    have front : ∀ (k : Ω[B⁄A]) (w : Fin q → Ω[B⁄A]), π k = 0 →
        exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (Fin.cons k w) ∈ Nsub := by
      intro k w hk
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨k, exteriorPower.ιMulti B q w, hk,
        by rw [coe_ιMulti_cons, coe_ιMulti_one]⟩
    by_cases h0 : i = 0
    · subst h0
      have hu : u = Fin.cons (u 0) (fun j => u j.succ) := by
        funext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ ?_ j <;> simp
      rw [hu]
      exact front (u 0) _ (by rw [← LinearMap.mem_ker]; rw [hu] at hi; simpa using hi)
    · have hswap : exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (u ∘ Equiv.swap 0 i)
          = - exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) u :=
        (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1)).map_swap u (Ne.symm h0)
      have hcons : u ∘ Equiv.swap 0 i = Fin.cons (u i) (fun j => (u ∘ Equiv.swap 0 i) j.succ) := by
        funext j; refine Fin.cases ?_ ?_ j
        · simp [Equiv.swap_apply_left]
        · intro j; simp
      have hmem : exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (u ∘ Equiv.swap 0 i) ∈ Nsub := by
        rw [hcons]; exact front (u i) _ (by rw [← LinearMap.mem_ker]; exact hi)
      rw [hswap] at hmem
      exact (Submodule.neg_mem_iff _).mp hmem
  have hslot_eq : ∀ [DecidableEq (Fin (q+1))] (u : Fin (q+1) → Ω[B⁄A]) (i : Fin (q+1))
      (α β : Ω[B⁄A]), α - β ∈ LinearMap.ker π →
      Submodule.Quotient.mk (p := Nsub) (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (Function.update u i α))
        = Submodule.Quotient.mk (p := Nsub)
            (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (Function.update u i β)) := by
    intro _ u i α β hk
    rw [← sub_eq_zero, ← Submodule.Quotient.mk_sub]
    have hsub : exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (Function.update u i α)
        - exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (Function.update u i β)
        = exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (Function.update u i (α - β)) := by
      have h := (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1)).toMultilinearMap.map_update_sub u i α β
      simp only [AlternatingMap.coe_multilinearMap] at h
      exact h.symm
    rw [hsub, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
    apply memN_slot _ i
    rwa [Function.update_self]
  have hsec_update : ∀ [DecidableEq (Fin (q+1))] (w : Fin (q+1) → Ω) (i : Fin (q+1)) (x : Ω),
      (fun j => sec (Function.update w i x j))
        = Function.update (fun j => sec (w j)) i (sec x) := by
    intro _ w i x; funext j; by_cases h : j = i
    · subst h; simp
    · simp [Function.update_of_ne h]
  let F : Ω [⋀^Fin (q+1)]→ₗ[B] ((⋀[B]^(q+1) (Ω[B⁄A])) ⧸ Nsub) :=
    AlternatingMap.mk
      { toFun := fun w => Submodule.Quotient.mk (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (fun i => sec (w i)))
        map_update_add' := by
          intro _ w i a b
          have hf := hsec_update w i
          rw [hf (a+b), hf a, hf b]
          set u := (fun j => sec (w j)) with hu
          rw [hslot_eq u i (sec (a+b)) (sec a + sec b)
            (by rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, map_sub, hs, map_add, hs, hs]; abel)]
          rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_add]
          congr 1
          have h :=
            (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1)).toMultilinearMap.map_update_add u i (sec a) (sec b)
          simp only [AlternatingMap.coe_multilinearMap] at h
          exact h
        map_update_smul' := by
          intro _ w i c a
          have hf := hsec_update w i
          rw [hf (c • a), hf a]
          set u := (fun j => sec (w j)) with hu
          rw [hslot_eq u i (sec (c • a)) (c • sec a)
            (by rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, map_sub, hs, map_smul, hs]; abel)]
          rw [← Submodule.Quotient.mk_smul]
          congr 1
          have h := (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1)).toMultilinearMap.map_update_smul u i c (sec a)
          simp only [AlternatingMap.coe_multilinearMap] at h
          exact h }
      (by
        intro w i j hij hne
        simp only
        rw [Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero]
        have heq : (fun k => sec (w k)) i = (fun k => sec (w k)) j := by simp only; rw [hij]
        rw [show exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (fun k => sec (w k)) = 0 from
          (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1)).map_eq_zero_of_eq _ heq hne]
        exact Submodule.zero_mem _)
  set g := exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv F with hg
  have telescope : ∀ (a a' : Fin (q+1) → Ω[B⁄A]), (∀ i, a' i - a i ∈ LinearMap.ker π) →
      Submodule.Quotient.mk (p := Nsub) (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) a')
        = Submodule.Quotient.mk (p := Nsub) (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) a) := by
    intro u u' hdiff
    have P : ∀ m : ℕ, Submodule.Quotient.mk (p := Nsub)
        (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (fun i : Fin (q+1) => if (i : ℕ) < m then u' i else u i))
        = Submodule.Quotient.mk (p := Nsub) (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) u) := by
      intro m
      induction m with
      | zero => simp
      | succ k ih =>
          by_cases hk : k < q + 1
          · have hupd_succ : (fun i : Fin (q+1) => if (i:ℕ) < k+1 then u' i else u i)
                = Function.update (fun i : Fin (q+1) => if (i:ℕ) < k then u' i else u i)
                    ⟨k, hk⟩ (u' ⟨k, hk⟩) := by
              funext i
              by_cases hik : i = ⟨k, hk⟩
              · subst hik; simp
              · rw [Function.update_of_ne hik]
                have hne : (i : ℕ) ≠ k := by intro h; exact hik (Fin.ext h)
                by_cases hlt : (i:ℕ) < k
                · simp [hlt, Nat.lt_succ_of_lt hlt]
                · have h2 : ¬ (i:ℕ) < k + 1 := by omega
                  simp [hlt, h2]
            have hupd_k : (fun i : Fin (q+1) => if (i:ℕ) < k then u' i else u i)
                = Function.update (fun i : Fin (q+1) => if (i:ℕ) < k then u' i else u i)
                    ⟨k, hk⟩ (u ⟨k, hk⟩) := by
              funext i
              by_cases hik : i = ⟨k, hk⟩
              · subst hik; simp
              · rw [Function.update_of_ne hik]
            rw [hupd_succ]
            rw [hslot_eq _ ⟨k, hk⟩ (u' ⟨k, hk⟩) (u ⟨k, hk⟩) (hdiff _)]
            rw [← hupd_k, ih]
          · have heq2 : (fun i : Fin (q+1) => if (i:ℕ) < k+1 then u' i else u i)
                = (fun i : Fin (q+1) => if (i:ℕ) < k then u' i else u i) := by
              funext i
              have hlt2 : (i:ℕ) < q + 1 := i.isLt
              by_cases hlt : (i:ℕ) < k
              · simp [hlt, Nat.lt_succ_of_lt hlt]
              · have h1 : ¬ (i:ℕ) < k + 1 := by omega
                simp [hlt, h1]
            rw [heq2, ih]
    have h1 := P (q+1)
    have heqf : (fun i : Fin (q+1) => if (i:ℕ) < q+1 then u' i else u i) = u' := by
      funext i; have : (i:ℕ) < q+1 := i.isLt; simp [this]
    rw [heqf] at h1
    exact h1
  have key : (g.comp (exteriorPower.map (q+1) π)) = Nsub.mkQ := by
    apply exteriorPower.linearMap_ext
    apply AlternatingMap.ext
    intro v
    simp only [LinearMap.compAlternatingMap_apply, LinearMap.comp_apply]
    rw [exteriorPower.map_apply_ιMulti]
    rw [hg, exteriorPower.alternatingMapLinearEquiv_apply_ιMulti]
    show Submodule.Quotient.mk (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) (fun i => sec ((π ∘ v) i)))
        = Nsub.mkQ (exteriorPower.ιMulti B (q+1) v)
    rw [Submodule.mkQ_apply]
    apply telescope
    intro i
    rw [LinearMap.mem_ker]
    simp only [Function.comp_apply, map_sub, hs, sub_self]
  intro x hx
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker] at hx
  have hxq : Nsub.mkQ x = 0 := by
    rw [← key]
    simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, hx, map_zero]
  rwa [Submodule.mkQ_apply, Submodule.Quotient.mk_eq_zero] at hxq

/-- `∧^{q+2} π` annihilates the source differential of a wedge `ω ∧ ζ` with `π ω = 0`. -/
private theorem map_d_wedge_eq_zero (hgen : S.GenerationHypothesis π) (q : ℕ)
    (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) (ζ : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])) (hω : π ω = 0)
    (z : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]))
    (hz : (z : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
      = (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
          * (ζ : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))) :
    exteriorPower.map (q + 2) π (S.d (q + 1) z) = 0 := by
  have compat : ∀ (n : ℕ) (w : ⋀[B]^n (Ω[B⁄A])),
      ((exteriorPower.map n π w : ⋀[B]^n Ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B Ω)
        = ExteriorAlgebra.map π (w : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) := by
    intro n w
    have hw : w ∈ (⊤ : Submodule B (⋀[B]^n (Ω[B⁄A]))) := Submodule.mem_top
    rw [← exteriorPower.ιMulti_span B n (Ω[B⁄A])] at hw
    induction hw using Submodule.span_induction with
    | mem x hx =>
        obtain ⟨m, rfl⟩ := hx
        rw [exteriorPower.map_apply_ιMulti, exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe,
          exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe, ExteriorAlgebra.map_apply_ιMulti]
    | zero => simp
    | add x y _ _ ihx ihy =>
        rw [map_add, Submodule.coe_add, Submodule.coe_add, map_add, ihx, ihy]
    | smul c x _ ih =>
        rw [map_smul, Submodule.coe_smul, Submodule.coe_smul, map_smul, ih]
  rw [← Submodule.coe_eq_zero, compat (q + 2) (S.d (q + 1) z)]
  rw [S.coe_d_wedge_one q ω ζ z hz]
  rw [map_sub, map_mul, map_mul]
  have hT1 : ExteriorAlgebra.map π
      ((S.d 1 ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm ω) : ⋀[B]^2 (Ω[B⁄A])).val
        : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) = 0 := by
    have hk : exteriorPower.map 1 π ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm ω) = 0 :=
      (exteriorPower.oneEquiv B Ω).injective
        (by rw [oneEquiv_map, LinearEquiv.apply_symm_apply, hω, map_zero])
    have hz1 : exteriorPower.map 2 π (S.d 1 ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm ω)) = 0 :=
      S.map_d_eq_zero_of_one π hgen _ hk
    rw [← compat 2 (S.d 1 ((exteriorPower.oneEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).symm ω)), hz1,
      Submodule.coe_zero]
  have hT2 : ExteriorAlgebra.map π
      (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) = 0 := by
    rw [exteriorPower.ιMulti_apply_coe, ExteriorAlgebra.map_apply_ιMulti]
    rw [show (⇑π ∘ fun _ : Fin 1 => ω) = (fun _ : Fin 1 => π ω) from rfl, hω]
    exact (ExteriorAlgebra.ιMulti B 1).map_coord_zero (i := 0) rfl
  rw [hT1, hT2, zero_mul, zero_mul, sub_zero]

/-- In degrees `p ≥ 2` the source differential carries `ker (∧^p π)` into `ker (∧^{p+1} π)`. -/
private theorem map_d_eq_zero_of_succ (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (hgen : S.GenerationHypothesis π)
    (q : ℕ) (x : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]))
    (hx : exteriorPower.map (q + 1) π x = 0) :
    exteriorPower.map (q + 1 + 1) π (S.d (q + 1) x) = 0 := by
  classical
  set T : Set (⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])) :=
    {z : ⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A]) |
      ∃ (ω : Ω[B⁄A]) (ζ : ⋀[B]^q (Ω[B⁄A])), π ω = 0 ∧
        (z : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
          = (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
              * (ζ : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))}
  have hmem : x ∈ Submodule.span B T :=
    ker_exteriorPower_map_le_span π hπ q (LinearMap.mem_ker.mpr hx)
  have hTsmul : ∀ (c : B), ∀ z ∈ T, c • z ∈ T := by
    intro c z hz
    obtain ⟨ω, ζ, hω, hcoe⟩ := hz
    refine ⟨c • ω, ζ, by rw [map_smul, hω, smul_zero], ?_⟩
    have hι : (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => c • ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A]))
        = c • (exteriorPower.ιMulti B 1 (fun _ => ω) : ExteriorAlgebra B (Ω[B⁄A])) := by
      simp
    rw [Submodule.coe_smul, hcoe, hι, smul_mul_assoc]
  have hclos_smul : ∀ (c : B), ∀ z ∈ AddSubmonoid.closure T, c • z ∈ AddSubmonoid.closure T := by
    intro c z hz
    induction hz using AddSubmonoid.closure_induction with
    | mem w hw => exact AddSubmonoid.subset_closure (hTsmul c w hw)
    | zero => rw [smul_zero]; exact (AddSubmonoid.closure T).zero_mem
    | add a b _ _ iha ihb => rw [smul_add]; exact (AddSubmonoid.closure T).add_mem iha ihb
  set M : Submodule B (⋀[B]^(q + 1) (Ω[B⁄A])) :=
    { AddSubmonoid.closure T with smul_mem' := fun c z hz => hclos_smul c z hz }
  have hxM : x ∈ AddSubmonoid.closure T := by
    have hle : Submodule.span B T ≤ M :=
      Submodule.span_le.mpr (fun z hz => AddSubmonoid.subset_closure hz)
    exact hle hmem
  clear hmem hx
  induction hxM using AddSubmonoid.closure_induction with
  | mem w hw =>
      obtain ⟨ω, ζ, hω, hcoe⟩ := hw
      exact S.map_d_wedge_eq_zero π hgen q ω ζ hω w hcoe
  | zero => simp
  | add a b _ _ iha ihb =>
      simp only [map_add, iha, ihb, add_zero]

/-- In every degree the source differential carries `ker (∧^p π)` into `ker (∧^{p+1} π)`. -/
private theorem map_d_eq_zero (hπ : Function.Surjective π) (hgen : S.GenerationHypothesis π)
    (p : ℕ) (x : ⋀[B]^p (Ω[B⁄A])) (hx : exteriorPower.map p π x = 0) :
    exteriorPower.map (p + 1) π (S.d p x) = 0 := by
  match p, x, hx with
  | 0, x, hx =>
      have hx0 : x = 0 := by
        have hnat := LinearMap.congr_fun (exteriorPower.zeroEquiv_naturality π) x
        simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe] at hnat
        rw [hx, map_zero] at hnat
        exact (exteriorPower.zeroEquiv B (Ω[B⁄A])).injective (by rw [map_zero]; exact hnat.symm)
      rw [hx0, map_zero, map_zero]
  | 1, x, hx =>
      exact S.map_d_eq_zero_of_one π hgen x hx
  | (q + 2), x, hx =>
      exact S.map_d_eq_zero_of_succ π hπ hgen (q + 1) x hx

/-- `ker (∧^p π) ≤ ker ((∧^{p+1} π) ∘ d_{B/A})`, which is what makes the descended
differentials well defined. -/
private theorem ker_mapA_le_ker_mapACompD (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hgen : S.GenerationHypothesis π) :
    ∀ p, LinearMap.ker (mapA π p) ≤ LinearMap.ker (S.mapACompD π p) := by
  intro p x hx
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, mapA_apply] at hx
  rw [LinearMap.mem_ker, mapACompD_apply]
  exact S.map_d_eq_zero π hπ hgen p x hx

end SourceDeRham

end Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent

open Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent Stacks.DeRham.DifferentialDescent.SourceDeRham in
/-- **Stacks 07HY.** Let `S` be the de Rham complex of `B` over `A` and let
`π : Ω[B⁄A] → Ω` be a surjection of `B`-modules whose kernel is generated by elements `ω` with
`π ω = 0` and `(⋀^2 π) (d ω) = 0`.  Then there is exactly one family of `A`-linear maps
`Ω^p = ⋀[B]^p Ω → Ω^{p+1}` making the squares `d ∘ (⋀^p π) = (⋀^{p+1} π) ∘ d_{B/A}` commute;
it obeys the same rule `d (f₀ · d f₁ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d f_p) = d f₀ ∧ ⋯ ∧ d f_p` on generators, with
`d f = π (d_{B/A} f)`, and it is again a complex. -/
@[stacks 07HY]
theorem exists_unique_quotient_deRhamDifferential
    (S : SourceDeRham A B)
    {Ω : Type u} [AddCommGroup Ω] [Module B Ω] (π : Ω[B⁄A] →ₗ[B] Ω)
    (hπ : Function.Surjective π)
    (hgen : S.GenerationHypothesis π) :
    ∃ dΩ : (∀ p, TgtA A B Ω p →ₗ[A] TgtA A B Ω (p + 1)),
      S.Commutes π dΩ ∧
      SatisfiesRule π dΩ ∧
      (∀ dΩ' : (∀ p, TgtA A B Ω p →ₗ[A] TgtA A B Ω (p + 1)), S.Commutes π dΩ' → dΩ' = dΩ) ∧
      (∀ p, (dΩ (p + 1)).comp (dΩ p) = 0) := by
  have hqsurj : ∀ p, Function.Surjective (mapA π p) := fun p => mapA_surjective π hπ p
  have hker : ∀ p, LinearMap.ker (mapA π p) ≤ LinearMap.ker (S.mapACompD π p) :=
    S.ker_mapA_le_ker_mapACompD π hπ hgen
  have hlift : ∀ (p : ℕ) (x : SrcA A B p),
      liftOfSurjective (mapA π p) (hqsurj p) (S.mapACompD π p) (hker p) (mapA π p x)
        = exteriorPower.map (p + 1) π (S.d p x) := fun p x => by
    have h := liftOfSurjective_apply (mapA π p) (hqsurj p) (S.mapACompD π p) (hker p) x
    rwa [mapACompD_apply] at h
  refine ⟨fun p => liftOfSurjective (mapA π p) (hqsurj p) (S.mapACompD π p) (hker p),
    fun p x => hlift p x, fun p b => ?_, fun dΩ' hcom' => ?_, fun p => LinearMap.ext fun y => ?_⟩
  · have hgen1 : exteriorPower.map p π (srcGen p b) = tgtGen π p b := by
      simp only [srcGen, tgtGen, map_smul, exteriorPower.map_apply_ιMulti]; rfl
    have hgen2 : exteriorPower.map (p + 1) π (srcGenRes p b) = tgtGenRes π p b := by
      simp only [srcGenRes, tgtGenRes, exteriorPower.map_apply_ιMulti]; rfl
    rw [← hgen1, ← mapA_apply, hlift p (srcGen p b), S.gen p b, hgen2]
  · refine funext fun p => LinearMap.ext fun y => ?_
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hqsurj p y
    rw [mapA_apply, hcom' p x, ← hlift p x, mapA_apply]
  · obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hqsurj p y
    have hcc : S.d (p + 1) (S.d p x) = 0 := by
      simpa using congrArg (fun g => g x) (S.complex p)
    rw [LinearMap.comp_apply, hlift p x, ← mapA_apply, hlift (p + 1) (S.d p x), hcc, map_zero,
      LinearMap.zero_apply]
